export default [{"id":"k1","title":"About Visionbotix","url":"https://visionbotix.com/about/","text":"Visionbotix is an AI-first product engineering studio. We build AI agents that do real work, plus the web, mobile and SaaS software they run in, with security built in."},{"id":"k2","title":"Visionbotix: Facts","url":"https://visionbotix.com/about/","text":"Facts: founded 2020; team of 30; 50+ projects delivered by our team for clients in 20 countries, including the USA, the UK, Germany, Switzerland, Austria, Australia, New Zealand, the UAE. Office: 2nd Floor, Meridian Software Technology Park, Satellite Town, Murree Road, Rawalpindi, Pakistan. Legal name: Visionbotix SMC-Private Limited. Founder: Sikandar Farooq."},{"id":"k3","title":"Visionbotix: Contact","url":"https://visionbotix.com/about/","text":"Contact: info@visionbotix.com · +92 51 8896050 · https://visionbotix.com/contact/ (fixed quote within 24 hours of a call)."},{"id":"k4","title":"Visionbotix: Pricing","url":"https://visionbotix.com/pricing/","text":"Pricing (USD, \"from\"): packaged AI agents from $750 setup + $199/month; AI Opportunity Audit $490; dedicated engineers from $2,200/month, hourly from $25. Details: https://visionbotix.com/pricing/"},{"id":"k5","title":"Visionbotix: Typical project costs","url":"https://visionbotix.com/estimate/","text":"Typical project costs (indicative ranges from our price list; a fixed quote follows a call): business website or simple web app $4,500–$7,000 (4–6 weeks); web app with accounts, payments and an admin $12,000–$18,000 (6–10 weeks); mobile app for ios and android $17,900–$27,000 (7–12 weeks); saas mvp with subscriptions $24,100–$36,000 (8–13 weeks); ai chatbot over your documents $7,500–$11,500 (5–8 weeks); custom ai agent that uses your systems $14,500–$22,000 (7–11 weeks); computer vision or iot prototype $10,000–$15,000 (5–8 weeks); clinic front desk (3 ai agents) $3,000–$4,000 setup + $699/mo (live in 2–5 weeks). Estimator: https://visionbotix.com/estimate/"},{"id":"k6","title":"Visionbotix: Promises","url":"https://visionbotix.com/about/","text":"Promises: NDA from the first call; the client owns 100% of the code and IP; fixed price or monthly, paid by milestone; overlap hours with the US, UK, Europe, the Gulf and Australia; weekly demos; 30 days of post-launch support."},{"id":"k7","title":"Packaged AI agents: Receptionist Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $349/mo. Our Receptionist Agent is an AI voice receptionist that answers your phone line 24/7 in your business's voice. It answers questions, books, moves and cancels appointments in your calendar or practice system, takes messages and puts urgent calls through to a person. Clinics, dental practices, salons and home-service firms go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k8","title":"Receptionist Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: How is an AI receptionist different from an answering service or a phone menu? A: An answering service takes a message and a phone menu makes callers press buttons. An AI receptionist holds a real conversation, answers questions from your own information and books the appointment during the call, at any hour and on several calls at once. Q: Will callers know they are speaking to an AI? A: Yes. We configure a clear, friendly disclosure in the greeting, and callers can ask for a person at any time. Being upfront builds trust and keeps you on the right side of disclosure rules."},{"id":"k9","title":"Receptionist Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: What happens with urgent or complicated calls? A: You decide the rules. Calls that match them, such as urgent symptoms, complaints or a request for a named person, are transferred live or flagged to your on-call team by text with a short summary, so a human takes over. Q: Can it use my existing phone number? A: Yes. You keep your number and forward calls to the agent, either all calls, only after hours or only when your lines are busy. We can also set up a new local number in most countries."},{"id":"k10","title":"Receptionist Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Which calendars and practice systems does it work with? A: Google Calendar, Outlook, Calendly and Cal.com out of the box, plus practice and CRM systems such as Open Dental, Cliniko, HubSpot and Salesforce. If your system has an API, we can connect it. Q: Which languages does it speak? A: English by default, with natural accents. Arabic, Urdu, Spanish, German, French and other major languages are available, and the agent can switch language when the caller does."},{"id":"k11","title":"Receptionist Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Is it suitable for healthcare data under HIPAA or UK GDPR? A: Yes, with the right setup. We keep data in your chosen region, encrypt it, apply your retention rules and, for US healthcare, use providers that sign a BAA. We document the data flow so your compliance lead can sign it off."},{"id":"k12","title":"Packaged AI agents: Support Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Price: From $2,500 + $449/mo. Our Support Agent is an AI customer support agent that resolves tier-1 tickets on website chat, email and WhatsApp, 24/7. It answers from your help center, policies and order data, handles actions like order lookups and returns, and hands anything sensitive to your team with full context. Online stores, SaaS and service businesses go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k13","title":"Support Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Q: How is an AI customer support agent different from a chatbot? A: A classic chatbot follows a decision tree and breaks as soon as a question doesn't fit it. An AI support agent understands free-text questions, answers from your own docs and can take actions in your systems, such as looking up an order or starting a return, then hands off when it should. Q: What stops it from making things up? A: It answers only from the sources you approve, such as your help center, policies and order data, and attaches the source to each answer. If the answer isn't in those sources, it says so and passes the ticket to your team. We test it on your real past tickets before launch."},{"id":"k14","title":"Support Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Q: What happens when it can't solve the problem? A: It hands the conversation to the right queue in your help desk with a short summary, the customer details and what it already tried, so your agent doesn't start from zero. Customers can also ask for a person at any time. Q: Does it work with our help desk? A: Yes. We connect Zendesk, Freshdesk, Intercom, HubSpot, Gorgias, Help Scout and Salesforce Service Cloud, and the agent works inside your existing queues and tags. If your system has an API, we can connect it."},{"id":"k15","title":"Support Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Q: Which languages does it support? A: English by default, plus Arabic, Urdu, Spanish, French, German and other major languages. It replies in the language the customer writes in, and answers still come from your approved docs. Q: Will it replace my support team? A: No. It takes the repetitive tier-1 tickets so your team can spend its time on complex cases, upset customers and the conversations that keep accounts. Refunds and other sensitive actions still need a person to approve them."},{"id":"k16","title":"Support Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Q: How much work is setup for my team? A: Expect a kickoff call, access to your help desk and docs, and a few short review sessions while we test it on real tickets. We do the configuration, connections and testing."},{"id":"k17","title":"Packaged AI agents: WhatsApp Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $299/mo. Our WhatsApp Agent is an AI agent for the WhatsApp Business Platform and Instagram DMs. It replies in seconds in English, Arabic, Urdu and more, answers product questions from your catalog, shares live order status, follows up abandoned carts with approved templates and passes complex chats to your team. Online stores, clinics and service brands go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k18","title":"WhatsApp Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Is this allowed by WhatsApp, and could my number get banned? A: We build on the official WhatsApp Business Platform, not unofficial automation tools, which is what puts numbers at risk. We follow Meta's rules on opt-in, the 24-hour reply window and approved templates, and we watch your quality rating so marketing messages stay welcome. Q: Can it reply in Arabic and Urdu? A: Yes. It replies in the language the customer writes in, including Arabic, Urdu and Roman Urdu, as well as English and other major languages. Answers still come from your approved catalog and policies, and we review the tone in each language with you."},{"id":"k19","title":"WhatsApp Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Can I keep my existing WhatsApp number? A: In most cases, yes. We connect your number to the WhatsApp Business Platform, and depending on your setup you can keep using the WhatsApp Business app on the same number alongside the agent. If that doesn't suit, we set up a new number for you. Q: What happens when a customer wants a real person? A: They can ask at any time. The chat moves to your team's shared inbox with the full history and order details, and the agent stays quiet until your team hands it back."},{"id":"k20","title":"WhatsApp Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Does it also work on Instagram? A: Yes. The same agent answers Instagram direct messages with the same catalog, rules and handoff, so customers get the same answer wherever they ask. Q: Which stores and couriers does it connect to? A: Shopify, WooCommerce, Magento, Salla and Zid out of the box, plus couriers such as Aramex and DHL Express. If your store or courier has an API, we can connect it."},{"id":"k21","title":"WhatsApp Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: What if it gives a customer a wrong answer? A: It only answers from your store data and approved knowledge base, and every chat is logged so you can see exactly what it said and why. When you correct a fact, the fix applies to every future conversation, and we review chats with you weekly."},{"id":"k22","title":"Packaged AI agents: Booking Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $299/mo. Our Booking Agent is an AI appointment setter that contacts every new lead from your forms, ads and portals within 60 seconds, by text, WhatsApp or call. It asks your qualifying questions, books qualified leads into the right calendar, sends reminders to cut no-shows and logs everything in your CRM. Real estate, clinic and home-service teams go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k23","title":"Booking Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Q: How is the Booking Agent different from the AI Receptionist? A: The Receptionist answers calls that come in to you. The Booking Agent reaches out to new leads from your forms, ads and portals within 60 seconds, qualifies them and books the appointment. Many businesses use both, one for inbound calls and one for speed-to-lead. Q: Is it legal to text and call leads automatically? A: It can be, when the lead has given the right consent. We set the agent up to contact only leads with consent on record, to name your business, respect quiet hours and honor opt-outs immediately, following TCPA in the US and GDPR and PECR in the UK and EU. Your legal advisor should confirm the consent wording on your forms."},{"id":"k24","title":"Booking Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Q: Will leads know they are talking to an AI? A: Yes, if they ask, and you can add a short disclosure to the first message. The agent never claims to be a person, and anyone can ask to speak to your team at any time. Q: Which lead sources and CRMs does it work with? A: Meta, Google and TikTok lead forms, your website forms, and CRMs such as HubSpot, Salesforce, GoHighLevel, Follow Up Boss, Zoho and Pipedrive. Portals that send leads by email or webhook can be connected too. If your system has an API, we can connect it."},{"id":"k25","title":"Booking Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Q: What happens if a lead asks something the agent can't answer? A: It tells the lead a team member will follow up, logs the question in your CRM and alerts the right person. It does not guess prices, availability or terms that are not in your approved information. Q: Can it call leads as well as text them? A: Yes. You choose the channel per source, for example a text first and a call if there is no reply, or a call straight away for high-value leads. Calls use a natural voice and can be transferred live to your team."},{"id":"k26","title":"Booking Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Q: Which languages does it work in? A: English by default, plus Arabic, Urdu, Spanish, French and other major languages. It can follow the language the lead uses on the form or in their reply."},{"id":"k27","title":"Packaged AI agents: SDR Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Price: From $2,500 + $499/mo. Our SDR Agent is an AI sales development rep for B2B teams. It researches each target account, finds the right contacts, writes personalized emails and LinkedIn drafts, handles replies and books meetings into your reps' calendars, with everything logged in your CRM. Your team approves every sequence before it sends. SaaS companies and agencies go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k28","title":"SDR Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Q: Will prospects know the emails were written with AI? A: Every email is reviewed and approved by your rep and sent from their inbox, so it is your team's message. When the agent handles replies, it never claims to be a person if asked, and you can add a short disclosure if you prefer. Q: Will it hurt our email deliverability? A: It's designed to protect it. We set daily sending limits, warm up inboxes, use suppression lists and keep volumes steady, and because each email is specific to the account, it reads like a real message, not a blast. We can also set up separate sending domains so your main domain stays clean."},{"id":"k29","title":"SDR Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Q: How personalized is the outreach really? A: Each first email is built on research about that account, such as a new location, an open role or a recent announcement, and connects it to a problem you solve. Your rep sees the research behind every draft and can edit anything before approving. Q: Does it automate LinkedIn? A: No. Automating LinkedIn accounts breaks LinkedIn's terms and puts your reps' profiles at risk. The agent drafts LinkedIn messages and connection notes for your reps to send themselves."},{"id":"k30","title":"SDR Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Q: Which CRMs and data providers does it work with? A: HubSpot, Salesforce, Pipedrive and Close for CRM, Apollo.io and Hunter for contact data, and Outreach or Salesloft if you already use them for sequencing. If your tool has an API, we can connect it. Q: Is cold B2B outreach allowed under GDPR? A: In many cases, yes, when it is relevant to the person's role, identifies your company, offers an easy opt-out and rests on a documented legitimate interest. We build those safeguards in, and your legal advisor should confirm the approach for your markets."},{"id":"k31","title":"SDR Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Q: What if it writes something wrong or off-brand? A: Nothing goes out without your rep's approval, and the agent only uses the claims and proof points you've signed off. When you edit a draft, we feed that back into the style guide so the next batch is closer to your voice."},{"id":"k32","title":"Packaged AI agents: Social Media Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,000 + $399/mo. Our Social Media Agent is an AI social media manager for businesses that need to post often but lack time. It plans a content calendar, writes captions, prepares on-brand graphics, schedules posts across your accounts and replies to comments and DMs in your voice. You approve the calendar, and sensitive replies go to your staff. Live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k33","title":"Social Media Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Q: How is an AI social media manager different from a scheduling tool like Buffer? A: A scheduler publishes what you give it. The agent also plans the calendar, writes the captions, prepares the graphics and answers comments and DMs. If you already use a scheduler, it can publish through it. Q: Will the posts sound like AI wrote them? A: We build a written voice guide from your best past posts and your feedback, and the agent drafts against it. You approve the calendar, so anything that doesn't sound like you is changed before it goes out, and we fold your edits back into the guide during weekly tuning."},{"id":"k34","title":"Social Media Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Q: Does it replace my social media manager or agency? A: It replaces the repetitive part, which is drafting, resizing, scheduling and first replies. Many teams keep a person for strategy, shoots and community moments, and that person spends their time on ideas instead of admin. Q: What happens if it replies with something wrong? A: Replies only use facts from your approved knowledge base, and anything sensitive, such as complaints, refunds or health and legal questions, goes to staff instead of getting an answer. Every reply is logged, so you can edit or delete it, and we fix the rule behind it in weekly tuning."},{"id":"k35","title":"Social Media Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Q: Which platforms does it support? A: Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, TikTok, X, YouTube, Pinterest and Google Business Profile, through their official APIs. Some features, such as DM replies on certain platforms, depend on what each platform allows for business accounts. Q: Is this allowed under the platforms' rules? A: Yes. It posts and replies through official business APIs with your permission, and it never buys engagement, runs fake accounts or sends unsolicited mass DMs. It also labels AI-generated images where a platform asks for it."},{"id":"k36","title":"Social Media Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Q: Can it create images and video? A: It produces graphics, carousels and simple motion from your brand templates and photos. For product shots and video it works best with real footage you supply, which it trims, captions and resizes for each platform."},{"id":"k37","title":"Packaged AI agents: SEO & GEO Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-seo-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $499/mo. Our SEO & GEO Agent is an AI SEO agent that covers classic search and generative engine optimization (GEO). It finds ranking and content gaps, drafts pages for your editor, flags technical fixes, and tracks how ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews and Copilot cite your brand. Built for B2B, SaaS, e-commerce and local businesses; live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k38","title":"SEO & GEO Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-seo-agent/","text":"Q: What is GEO, and how is it different from SEO? A: SEO helps your pages rank in classic search results. Generative engine optimization (GEO) helps AI assistants such as ChatGPT, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews understand, mention and cite your business when they answer a question. The foundations overlap, and GEO adds tracking of AI answers and pages written to be quoted. Q: Can I check my site's AI visibility before I talk to you? A: Yes. Our free AI visibility checker tests whether the crawlers behind ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Google and Bing may read your page, what text they see without JavaScript, and whether they can tell who you are. The agent starts from the same checks, then tracks real AI answers every month."},{"id":"k39","title":"SEO & GEO Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-seo-agent/","text":"Q: Can you guarantee rankings or AI citations? A: No, and nobody honestly can, because search engines and AI assistants decide what to show. What we commit to is the process, which is regular tracking, a prioritized task list, reviewed drafts and technical fixes, with a weekly report that shows what changed. Q: Will AI-written content hurt my site? A: Thin, mass-produced content can. The agent drafts pages around your real expertise, facts and examples, and an editor reviews every page before it is published. It never publishes in bulk on its own."},{"id":"k40","title":"SEO & GEO Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-seo-agent/","text":"Q: How do you track mentions in ChatGPT and Perplexity? A: We run a fixed set of buyer questions on a schedule across the major assistants and record whether you are mentioned, how you are described and which URLs are cited. AI answers vary from run to run, so we report trends over several weeks rather than a single result. Q: Does it replace my SEO agency or in-house marketer? A: It replaces the repetitive work of crawling, monitoring, research and first drafts. Strategy, subject expertise and final editing stay with your team or agency, who get more done because the groundwork is ready."},{"id":"k41","title":"SEO & GEO Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-seo-agent/","text":"Q: Which tools and CMS does it work with? A: Google Search Console, Analytics 4 and Business Profile, Bing Webmaster Tools, Ahrefs or Semrush if you use them, and WordPress, Webflow, Shopify or a Git-based site for drafts and fixes. If your CMS has an API, we can connect it."},{"id":"k42","title":"Packaged AI agents: Ads Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-ads-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $449/mo. Our Ads Agent is an AI ads agent that reviews your Meta and Google Ads accounts every morning. It spots wasted spend, pauses ads that break your rules, catches tracking problems and proposes budget moves. Anything above the thresholds you set waits for your approval. Built for e-commerce brands, lead-gen businesses and marketing teams; live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k43","title":"Ads Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-ads-agent/","text":"Q: Will it improve my ROAS? A: We don't promise ad results, because they depend on your offer, creative, market and budget. What the agent does is make sure no account goes a day without a check, losing ads are caught early and every budget move is backed by data you can see. Q: Can it spend my money without asking? A: Only within the limits you set. You decide what it may pause or shift on its own, per account and per day, and everything above that waits for your approval. It can never raise your total budget or touch billing."},{"id":"k44","title":"Ads Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-ads-agent/","text":"Q: How is this different from Google's and Meta's own automation? A: Platform automation optimizes inside one platform toward the goal you give it. The agent sits above both platforms, checks results against your business targets and real sales data, explains every proposal in plain language and asks before big changes. It works alongside Smart Bidding and Advantage+, not against them. Q: Does it replace my agency or media buyer? A: No. It takes over the daily watching and the paperwork, so your media buyer or agency spends time on strategy, creative and testing. Agencies also use it to check every client account each morning."},{"id":"k45","title":"Ads Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-ads-agent/","text":"Q: Which ad platforms does it support? A: Meta (Facebook and Instagram) and Google Ads out of the box, with Microsoft Advertising, LinkedIn Ads and TikTok Ads on request. It can also read GA4, Shopify or your CRM so it judges results by real sales or leads. Q: What if it makes a wrong call? A: Every action is logged with the before and after values, so any change can be reviewed and reversed quickly. You can also keep it in shadow mode, where it only proposes, until you trust its judgment."},{"id":"k46","title":"Packaged AI agents: Reputation Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Price: From $750 + $199/mo. Our Reputation Agent is an AI reputation management agent that watches your Google, Trustpilot and app-store reviews around the clock. It drafts specific, on-brand replies, holds negative reviews for your approval, alerts you to urgent issues and asks every recent customer for a review, within platform rules. Clinics, restaurants, hotels, online stores and apps go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k47","title":"Reputation Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Q: Is it allowed to use AI to reply to reviews? A: Yes. Google, Trustpilot and the app stores let businesses reply to reviews, and what matters is that replies are honest, relevant and respectful. We keep a person in the loop for every negative or sensitive reply, and you can require approval for all of them. Q: Can it remove or hide bad reviews? A: No, and nothing should. Genuine reviews stay up. The agent can flag reviews that appear to break platform policy, such as spam or reviews of the wrong business, so you can report them through the platform's own process."},{"id":"k48","title":"Reputation Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Q: Can it ask only happy customers for reviews? A: No. Asking only satisfied customers, known as review gating, is against Google's policies and FTC guidance in the US, and so are incentives for reviews. The agent asks every eligible customer in the same way, which keeps your profile trustworthy and your listing safe. Q: Which review platforms does it cover? A: Google Business Profile, Trustpilot, the App Store, Google Play and Facebook out of the box. Other platforms can be added where they offer an official API or review notifications, and where a platform doesn't allow replies through its API, the agent drafts the reply and your team posts it."},{"id":"k49","title":"Reputation Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Q: Will the replies sound robotic or repetitive? A: No. Each reply responds to what the reviewer actually wrote, follows your style guide and varies its wording. You can edit any draft, and your edits shape future replies. Q: How does it handle healthcare privacy? A: For clinics and practices, replies never confirm that the reviewer is a patient, mention treatment or share any details, even if the reviewer did. Negative reviews are always held for approval, and data stays in your chosen region."},{"id":"k50","title":"Reputation Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Q: What if it drafts something wrong? A: Sensitive replies don't post without a person approving them, and every draft, edit and approval is logged. If you correct a fact or a phrase, we add it to the style guide so it doesn't happen again."},{"id":"k51","title":"Packaged AI agents: Knowledge Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-knowledge-assistant/","text":"Price: From $3,500 + $399/mo. Our Knowledge Agent is a private AI knowledge assistant that answers your team's questions from your own documents, wiki, shared drives and tickets. Every answer cites its sources, and people only see what their existing permissions allow. It runs in your private cloud or on-premise for sensitive data. Built for operations, support, legal and engineering teams; live in 2–4 weeks."},{"id":"k52","title":"Knowledge Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-knowledge-assistant/","text":"Q: How does it avoid making things up? A: It uses retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), so it first finds the relevant passages in your documents and then answers only from them, citing each source. If the sources don't cover the question, it says it doesn't know. No AI is perfect, which is why every answer carries citations people can check in one click. Q: How is this different from ChatGPT Enterprise or Microsoft Copilot? A: Those are strong general assistants. The Knowledge Agent is built around your sources, with retrieval tuned to your documents, permissions mirrored across tools from different vendors, gap reports for document owners and the option to run fully on-premise. It can also run alongside Copilot."},{"id":"k53","title":"Knowledge Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-knowledge-assistant/","text":"Q: Can it run fully on-premise or air-gapped? A: Yes. We can deploy on your own servers with an open-weight model, so no document, question or answer leaves your network. Hosted models are stronger on some tasks, so we help you choose per use case. Q: Will people see documents they shouldn't? A: No. Permissions are checked at question time against your identity provider and each source's own access rules, so an answer can only draw on files that person can already open."},{"id":"k54","title":"Knowledge Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-knowledge-assistant/","text":"Q: Which sources can it connect to? A: SharePoint, OneDrive, Google Drive, Confluence, Notion, Jira, Zendesk, Box, Dropbox, GitHub and network file shares, plus databases and internal systems with an API. Scanned PDFs are read with OCR. Q: How much work is it for our team? A: A few hours in total, covering a kick-off call, access to the sources and a small group to test answers during setup. After launch, document owners spend a little time each month on the gap report."},{"id":"k55","title":"Packaged AI agents: Document Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Price: From $3,000 + $399/mo. Our Document Agent handles AI document processing for finance, operations and compliance teams. It reads invoices, receipts, contracts, claims and KYC documents from email, scans or uploads, extracts the fields you need, checks them against your rules and ERP data, and posts clean records. Anything uncertain goes to a human review queue. Live in 2–4 weeks."},{"id":"k56","title":"Document Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Q: How accurate is it? A: It depends on the document type and scan quality, so we measure it on a sample of your own past documents during setup and show you the results before go-live. Fields the agent is unsure about are never posted silently; they go to a person in the review queue. Q: How is this different from OCR software? A: OCR turns an image into text. The agent understands what the text means, so it finds the invoice number or renewal date in any layout, checks it against your rules and data, and posts the result. Template-based OCR needs a new template for each layout, and the agent does not."},{"id":"k57","title":"Document Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Q: What happens when it gets something wrong? A: Validation rules and confidence checks are there to stop a doubtful value before it is posted and send the document to a person instead. Corrections are logged and reviewed in weekly tuning, so the cause gets fixed rather than patched. Q: Does it replace our AP or onboarding team? A: It removes the retyping. Your team moves to reviewing exceptions, dealing with suppliers and customers, and approving payments, which is the work that needs judgment."},{"id":"k58","title":"Document Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Q: Which systems can it post to? A: NetSuite, Dynamics 365, SAP Business One, Xero, QuickBooks Online, Sage Intacct and Salesforce, plus most other ERP, CRM or case systems with an API. If a system has no API, the agent can produce validated import files instead. Q: Is it safe for ID documents and financial data? A: Yes, with the right setup. Data is encrypted, kept in your chosen region, masked in logs and deleted on your schedule, with private-cloud and on-premise options. For KYC, the agent prepares and checks the documents, and decisions about customers stay with your compliance team."},{"id":"k59","title":"Document Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Q: Which documents and languages does it handle? A: Invoices, receipts, purchase orders, contracts, claim forms, bank statements, IDs, utility bills and logistics documents, in English, Arabic and other major languages. Handwriting and poor scans are harder to read, so they go to review more often."},{"id":"k60","title":"Packaged AI agents: Ops Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-workflow-automation-agent/","text":"Price: From $2,000 + $299/mo. Our Ops Agent is AI workflow automation for the repetitive work between your email, spreadsheets, CRM and ERP. It reads emails and documents, updates records, routes requests and chases follow-ups, built on n8n, Make or custom code, whichever your team can maintain. Anything irreversible waits for human approval, every run is logged, and it goes live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k61","title":"Ops Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-workflow-automation-agent/","text":"Q: How is this different from Zapier or a normal automation? A: Rule-based automations follow fixed steps and break when an input changes shape. The Ops Agent adds AI steps that read unstructured emails and documents, make routing decisions and draft replies, while the plumbing stays in a proven workflow engine. You get the flexibility of AI with the predictability of a workflow. Q: Do you build on n8n, Make or custom code? A: Whichever your team can maintain. n8n suits teams that want to self-host and keep data in their own cloud, Make suits teams that want a visual tool with many ready connectors, and custom code suits high volumes or unusual systems. We recommend one in writing after mapping the process."},{"id":"k62","title":"Ops Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-workflow-automation-agent/","text":"Q: What happens if the AI gets something wrong? A: Every AI step has a confidence threshold, and anything below it goes to a person instead of into your systems. Irreversible actions always wait for approval, and every run is logged, so a mistake can be traced, fixed and rolled back. Q: Can it work with an older ERP that has no modern API? A: Often, yes. We can connect through database views, file drops, email or an existing integration layer. If a system has no safe way in, we tell you during mapping instead of building something fragile."},{"id":"k63","title":"Ops Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-workflow-automation-agent/","text":"Q: Who owns the workflows? A: You do. Workflows live in your own account or your self-hosted n8n, and each one is documented so your team or another provider can maintain it. Q: Which process should we automate first? A: Pick one that is frequent, rule-heavy and has a clear owner. Invoice intake, lead routing and customer onboarding are common first choices. We help you choose on the first call and add more once the first workflow is stable."},{"id":"k64","title":"Packaged AI agents: Data Analyst Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-data-analyst-agent/","text":"Price: From $3,000 + $399/mo. Our Data Analyst Agent is an AI data analyst that answers plain-English questions from your database, warehouse or BI tool. It writes read-only SQL against tables and views you approve, shows the query, a table and a chart, and sends scheduled summaries to Slack, Teams or email. Built for teams without a full-time analyst, it goes live in 2–3 weeks."},{"id":"k65","title":"Data Analyst Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-data-analyst-agent/","text":"Q: Can the agent change or delete our data? A: No. It connects with a read-only database user and can only see the tables and views you approve. Every query is logged, and limits on rows, time and warehouse cost stop anything heavy. Q: How do we know the answers are right? A: Every answer shows the SQL it ran, so it can be checked. Before launch we test the agent against your own questions with known answers, and we rerun that test after every change. When a term is ambiguous, the agent asks what you mean instead of guessing."},{"id":"k66","title":"Data Analyst Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-data-analyst-agent/","text":"Q: Do we need a data warehouse first? A: No. It works with a production database, a read replica, a warehouse or the database behind your BI tool. If it has to query production, we point it at a replica or set strict limits so it never slows your app. Q: What data does the AI model see? A: The schema descriptions, your question and the result rows needed to write the answer. Sensitive columns can be masked or excluded, providers are configured not to train on your data, and the model can run in the cloud region you choose."},{"id":"k67","title":"Data Analyst Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-data-analyst-agent/","text":"Q: How is this different from the AI built into Power BI or Looker? A: Built-in assistants work well inside one tool. The Data Analyst Agent works across your databases, uses definitions you approve, lives in Slack or Teams, and sends digests and alerts. If you already use a BI tool, it complements it rather than replacing it. Q: Will it replace our data analyst? A: No. It takes the quick ad hoc questions off your analyst's plate so they can spend time on deeper work. Many teams without an analyst use it to get answers they could not get before."},{"id":"k68","title":"Packaged AI agents: MCP Connector","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/mcp-server-development/","text":"Price: From $2,500. Our MCP Connector is an MCP server development service. We build Model Context Protocol servers that let Claude, ChatGPT and Microsoft Copilot read from and act on your internal systems: databases, CRM, ERP, ticketing and documents. Every server ships with least-privilege scopes, OAuth sign-in, rate limits, audit logs and approval for write actions. Delivered in 2–4 weeks as a one-off project."},{"id":"k69","title":"MCP Connector: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/mcp-server-development/","text":"Q: What is an MCP server? A: The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open standard, introduced by Anthropic and now supported by OpenAI, Microsoft and others, that lets AI apps connect to tools and data in one consistent way. An MCP server is the service that sits in front of your system and exposes a defined set of tools to an AI client. You build it once and use it from any client that supports MCP. Q: Why not just use an open-source MCP server from GitHub? A: Many are fine for personal use, but they often run with one broad token, have no per-user sign-in and keep no audit trail. For company data you need scopes, identity, approval steps and logs. We can harden an existing server or build one designed for your systems."},{"id":"k70","title":"MCP Connector: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/mcp-server-development/","text":"Q: Can the AI change data in our systems? A: Only through write tools you approve, and each write pauses for confirmation by the user or a named approver. Everything else is read-only by default, and a kill switch turns any tool off instantly. Q: Which AI clients will it work with? A: Claude (web, desktop and Claude Code), ChatGPT on plans that allow custom connectors, Microsoft Copilot Studio, and coding agents such as Cursor and VS Code. Client support changes quickly, so we test against the clients your team actually uses."},{"id":"k71","title":"MCP Connector: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/mcp-server-development/","text":"Q: Where does the MCP server run? A: In your own cloud on AWS, Azure or Google Cloud, or on-premises behind your gateway. Credentials and data stay in your environment, and only the results of approved tool calls go back to the AI client. Q: Is this a monthly subscription? A: No. The MCP Connector is a one-off project, and you own the code. An optional maintenance plan keeps it updated as the MCP specification, your systems and the AI clients change."},{"id":"k72","title":"Packaged AI agents: Guardrail & Eval Audit","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-security-audit/","text":"Price: From $2,500. Our Guardrail & Eval Audit is a fixed-price LLM security audit for AI apps, chatbots and agents. We red-team your system for prompt injection, jailbreaks, data and PII leakage, tool misuse and hallucination, map each finding to the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications, and deliver a written report with fixes and a CI eval suite. Report in about two weeks, retest included."},{"id":"k73","title":"Guardrail & Eval Audit: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-security-audit/","text":"Q: What is an LLM security audit? A: It is a structured attempt to break your AI app the way a real attacker or a careless user would. We test for prompt injection, jailbreaks, data leakage, tool misuse and hallucination, then report what we found, how serious it is and how to fix it. Q: How is this different from a normal penetration test? A: A penetration test looks at your network, servers and web app. An LLM audit looks at how the model behaves, what it can be talked into, what it retrieves and which tools it can call. The two complement each other, and we can cover both if you need them."},{"id":"k74","title":"Guardrail & Eval Audit: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-security-audit/","text":"Q: Which AI apps can you test? A: Chatbots, copilots, RAG search, document tools and agents with tool access, built on OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, Google Vertex AI or open models, with any framework. We need a staging environment or test tenant and accounts for each user role. Q: Will testing affect our customers or production systems? A: No, as long as we test on staging or a test tenant, which is our default. Rules of engagement set the scope and time windows, and anything that could trigger a real action runs against sandboxed tools."},{"id":"k75","title":"Guardrail & Eval Audit: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-security-audit/","text":"Q: Do you fix the issues as well? A: The report gives specific fixes for your architecture, and most teams apply them in-house. If you prefer, we can implement the fixes as a separate piece of work. Either way, the retest of every finding is included. Q: Does the audit make us compliant? A: No single test makes you compliant. The report and eval suite give your compliance team documented evidence of AI risk testing, mapped to the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications, which supports frameworks such as the NIST AI RMF, ISO/IEC 42001 and the EU AI Act."},{"id":"k76","title":"Packaged AI agents: AI MVP Sprint","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Price: From $12,000. Our AI MVP Sprint is fixed-price AI MVP development for founders and product teams. In 6–8 weeks we take your idea through discovery, a clickable prototype, the build (web app, AI features and evals) and launch, with a demo every week. Fixed scope, fixed price, an NDA from the first call, and you own 100% of the code and IP."},{"id":"k77","title":"AI MVP Sprint: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Q: What can realistically be built in 6–8 weeks? A: One core user journey done properly, with sign-in, an admin area and the AI features that make the product valuable. Discovery is there to cut everything else to a later list. Keeping the first version small is what keeps the date and the price fixed. Q: What if we need to change the scope during the sprint? A: Small changes are swapped in through a short change note, so something of similar size moves to the later list and the date and price hold. A larger change gets a written quote and a new date before any work starts, so there are no surprises."},{"id":"k78","title":"AI MVP Sprint: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Do I really own the code and IP? A: Yes, 100%. The code and IP are yours, the handover includes the repository, documentation and deployment access, and you can take the code to any team at any time. We can also set up the repository and cloud accounts in your name from the start if you prefer. Q: Which AI models do you use? A: Whichever fits the job on quality, speed, cost and data rules, usually OpenAI or Anthropic models, or an open model when data must stay in your cloud. We keep the model behind a thin layer and test it with evals, so you can switch later without a rewrite."},{"id":"k79","title":"AI MVP Sprint: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Will you sign an NDA before I share my idea? A: Yes. We sign an NDA from the first call, before you share any detail. Your idea, data and documents are only seen by the people working on your sprint. Q: Can you work with my CTO or in-house developers? A: Yes. Your developers can join the repository, review code and attend the weekly demos from the start, which makes the handover much smoother. Many teams use the sprint to get a solid base their own team then grows."},{"id":"k80","title":"AI MVP Sprint: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Q: What happens after launch? A: You get 30 days of post-launch support for fixes and small adjustments. After that, you can run the product with your own team, bring us back for the next version, or hire a dedicated team from us."},{"id":"k81","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Receptionist Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/receptionist/","text":"Talk to a real AI voice receptionist for a fictional dental clinic. Use your microphone or type. It answers questions, checks the calendar, books you in, escalates urgent cases and asks staff before it bends a rule. The trace beside the call shows every step and why it took it."},{"id":"k82","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Support Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/support/","text":"Chat with an AI support agent for a fictional online store. It answers from the help center with sources, checks your identity before it touches an order, starts returns and refunds, and asks a person to approve anything over its limit. Every step is in the trace."},{"id":"k83","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): WhatsApp Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/whatsapp/","text":"Chat with a WhatsApp-style AI agent for a fictional Dubai boutique, in English, Arabic or Urdu. It answers from the catalog, shares live order status, recovers an abandoned basket with a checkout link and checks with the manager before a big discount."},{"id":"k84","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Booking Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/booking/","text":"Send a sample enquiry to a fictional remodeling firm and the AI booking agent texts you back within seconds. It asks qualifying questions, books a free estimate on the calendar, schedules reminders and keeps the CRM record up to date, with a person approving anything outside the rules."},{"id":"k85","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): SDR Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/sdr/","text":"Pick a sample company and the AI SDR agent researches it, checks the fit, finds the right person (respecting a do-not-contact list) and drafts a short, specific email that must cite a real buying signal. Nothing goes out until you approve the sequence."},{"id":"k86","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Social Media Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/social/","text":"Brief the AI social media agent for a fictional Manchester pizzeria and it plans a week of Instagram and X posts in the brand voice, checks each one against platform limits and allergy rules, and answers comments. Posts and complaint replies wait for your approval."},{"id":"k87","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): SEO & GEO Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/seo/","text":"The AI SEO & GEO agent audits a fictional bike shop’s pages in code, shows keyword gaps and whether AI assistants cite the business, then drafts titles, descriptions and FAQs that are validated before you approve publishing."},{"id":"k88","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Ads Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/ads/","text":"The AI ads agent reads a sample Meta and Google Ads account, explains ROAS per campaign and proposes budget moves from losers to winners. Hard limits run in code (per-campaign change, total budget), and nothing changes until you approve."},{"id":"k89","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Reputation Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/reputation/","text":"The AI reputation agent drafts on-brand replies to a fictional café’s Google reviews, posts the positive ones, sends critical ones to the owner for approval, reports fake or spam reviews and asks every recent customer for a review, the way Google’s rules require."},{"id":"k90","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Knowledge Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/knowledge/","text":"Ask a fictional company’s policies anything: leave, expenses, travel, IT security. The AI knowledge assistant answers only from its sources, cites each one, says when it does not know, and hides manager-only sections from employees. It is the same RAG pattern we build over your own documents."},{"id":"k91","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Document Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/document/","text":"The AI document agent reads sample supplier invoices, extracts the fields into structured JSON and validates them in code: line maths, VAT, totals, purchase-order match and supplier. Clean small invoices post to the ERP; anything else waits for a person."},{"id":"k92","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Ops Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/ops/","text":"The AI ops agent runs a fictional print shop’s order-to-invoice workflow: it reads the email, matches the customer in the CRM, prices the job from the price list, creates the invoice, logs it, notifies the team and asks you before emailing the customer."},{"id":"k93","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Data Analyst Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/data/","text":"Ask a fictional coffee shop’s database anything: revenue by month, best sellers, customer countries. The AI data analyst writes the SQL, runs it on a real read-only database with personal data masked, and answers with a table and a chart."},{"id":"k94","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): MCP Connector live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/mcp/","text":"An AI assistant answers questions by calling a fictional company’s CRM, support tickets and docs through MCP servers. You see every JSON-RPC call, set the token’s scopes yourself, and approve any write. It is the same pattern we use to connect Claude, ChatGPT or Copilot to your systems."},{"id":"k95","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Guardrail & Eval Audit live dem","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/guardrail/","text":"A fictional bank’s AI assistant hides a secret code. Try any jailbreak you like. Four layers defend it: input checks with a prompt-injection classifier, hardened instructions, tools that verify in code, and an output filter. The scoreboard shows which layer stopped each attack."},{"id":"k96","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): AI MVP Sprint live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/mvp/","text":"Describe your AI product idea and our scoping agent interviews you, cuts it to a launchable MVP of five core features, lays out the build plan and prices it with the same estimator our team uses. A fixed quote follows a call."},{"id":"k97","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): All live demos","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/","text":"16 agents live on fictional businesses, with every tool call, guardrail and approval shown. A site concierge on every page answers questions about Visionbotix."},{"id":"k98","title":"Services: AI agent development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Price: From $8,000. Visionbotix builds custom AI agents that plan, use your tools and finish multi-step work, such as triaging tickets, reconciling records or preparing reports. Each agent connects to your systems through APIs or MCP, works behind guardrails and human approval gates, and ships with an eval suite and an audit log. Projects are fixed price, and you own the code."},{"id":"k99","title":"AI agent development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Q: What is the difference between an AI agent and a chatbot? A: A chatbot answers questions in a conversation. An AI agent takes actions to finish a task. It plans the steps, uses your tools such as the CRM, inbox or database, checks its own work and asks a person for approval when your rules require it. Q: Should we build a custom agent or use a packaged one? A: Start with a packaged agent when the job is common, such as answering calls, booking or support, because it goes live in about two weeks at a lower price. Build a custom agent when the work depends on your own systems, rules or data, or when the agent is part of your product."},{"id":"k100","title":"AI agent development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Q: Which models and frameworks do you use? A: We are model-agnostic. We choose between Claude, GPT, Gemini and open models such as Llama for each task based on quality, cost and your data rules, and we build with LangGraph, the OpenAI Agents SDK or plain code where that is simpler. The design lets you switch models later without a rebuild. Q: How do you stop an agent from making costly mistakes? A: Agents only get the tools and data their job needs, risky actions wait at an approval gate, and every step is in the audit log. Before launch the agent must pass an eval suite built from your real cases, and we re-run it after every change."},{"id":"k101","title":"AI agent development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Q: Can the agent run on our own infrastructure? A: Yes. We deploy in your AWS, Azure or Google Cloud account, on your own servers, or fully air-gapped with open models when data must never leave your network. Q: How long does it take to build a custom AI agent? A: A focused single-task agent is usually live in six to ten weeks, including a prototype on your real data in the first two to three weeks. Multi-agent systems are planned in milestones, and you see a working demo every week."},{"id":"k102","title":"AI agent development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Q: Do we own the agent and the code? A: Yes. The contract assigns 100% of the code, prompts, configuration and IP to you on payment, and the repository is yours, so you can run it with or without us."},{"id":"k103","title":"Services: Generative AI development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Price: From $6,000. Visionbotix builds generative AI applications for SaaS companies and data-heavy teams: LLM apps, RAG over company documents, fine-tuned models and AI features inside existing products. Every build ships with an eval suite, guardrails and cost controls, runs on the model that fits your data rules, and is fixed price, with 100% of the code yours."},{"id":"k104","title":"Generative AI development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Q: What does generative AI development include? A: It means building software around large language models that write, summarize, extract or answer from your data, such as a document Q&A tool, a drafting assistant or an AI feature in your SaaS. It differs from agent development in one way. A generative AI app produces an answer or a draft for a person, while an agent goes on to take actions in your systems. Q: Should we use RAG or fine-tuning? A: Use RAG when answers must come from facts that change and you need sources, such as policies, contracts or product data. Use fine-tuning when you need a fixed format or tone at high volume, or want a smaller model to do one narrow task cheaply. Most projects start with RAG and good prompts, and we fine-tune only when the evals show a gap that prompting cannot close."},{"id":"k105","title":"Generative AI development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Q: How do you stop the model from making things up? A: We ground answers in your retrieved content, require a citation for every claim and tell the model to say it does not know when the sources are silent. The eval suite measures how often answers stay faithful to the sources, and high-stakes outputs such as legal or medical text go to a person for review before they are used. Q: Will our data be used to train someone else's model? A: No. We use enterprise API terms that exclude your data from training, or deploy open models such as Llama or Mistral in your own cloud or on-premises when data must not leave your environment. Personal data can also be masked before any model sees it."},{"id":"k106","title":"Generative AI development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Q: Can we switch models later? A: Yes. We put a thin layer between your application and the model provider, so switching is a configuration change followed by an eval run. When a new model is released, we can score it on your own eval set before you decide to move. Q: Can you add generative AI to our existing product? A: Yes. We work in your repository and your stack, ship the feature behind a feature flag, keep each customer's data isolated and add usage limits so one tenant cannot run up the bill. Your engineers review every pull request, and we hand over documentation and the eval suite with the code."},{"id":"k107","title":"Generative AI development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Q: What happens after launch? A: The first 30 days of fixes and tuning are included. After that you can run it yourself with the eval suite and dashboards we hand over, or take a monthly plan where we watch quality and cost, re-run evals and tune retrieval and prompts as your content changes."},{"id":"k108","title":"Services: AI automation","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Price: From $2,000. Visionbotix is an AI automation agency for operations, finance and sales teams. We automate email triage, data entry, reporting and CRM or ERP sync using n8n, Make, Zapier or custom code, with AI steps for messy inputs and human approval for risky actions. Work is fixed price per workflow or monthly, and every workflow is yours."},{"id":"k109","title":"AI automation: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Q: What is the difference between AI automation and regular automation? A: Regular automation follows fixed rules, such as copying two fields from a form into the CRM. AI automation adds steps that understand unstructured input, like reading an email to work out what the customer wants or pulling totals from a scanned invoice. The workflow engine still controls the order of steps and the approvals, so results stay predictable. Q: Should we use n8n, Make, Zapier or custom code? A: Zapier is the quickest for simple flows between popular apps. Make handles visual flows with more branching, n8n suits teams that want to self-host and keep data in their own cloud, and custom code fits high volumes or systems without good connectors. We recommend one per workflow in writing, and many clients end up with a mix."},{"id":"k110","title":"AI automation: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Q: Our existing automations keep breaking. Can you fix them? A: Yes. We list what you have, document what each automation does, add error handling and alerts, and remove duplicates that fight each other. Fragile flows are rebuilt in a sturdier tool only where that is worth it. Q: Which processes should we automate first? A: The best first candidates happen every day, follow mostly the same steps and hurt when they are late, such as invoice entry, lead routing or the morning sales report. We rank your candidates during the process review by time saved and risk, and start with one that pays back quickly."},{"id":"k111","title":"AI automation: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Q: Will automation replace our staff? A: It replaces the repetitive steps, not the judgment. In most teams people move from typing and checking to handling exceptions, approvals and customers. We design each workflow with the people who do the job today, so it fits how they actually work. Q: Who maintains the workflows after launch? A: Your choice. Workflows live in your own accounts or your self-hosted n8n, with documentation your team can follow. If you would rather not maintain them, a monthly plan covers monitoring, fixes when a connected app changes, and new workflows as you need them."},{"id":"k112","title":"AI automation: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Q: Is our data safe in tools like Zapier and Make? A: Both process data in their own cloud, which is fine for many workflows. For sensitive data we use self-hosted n8n or custom code in your environment, mask personal data before any AI step and give each workflow only the access it needs."},{"id":"k113","title":"Services: AI chatbot development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Price: From $1,500. Visionbotix builds custom AI chatbots for support, sales and internal teams, on websites, help desks, WhatsApp, Instagram and Messenger. Each bot answers from your approved content, speaks English, Arabic, Urdu and other languages, and hands the conversation to a person with full context. Packaged chat agents go live in about two weeks; custom builds are fixed price."},{"id":"k114","title":"AI chatbot development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Q: What is the difference between a rule-based chatbot and an AI chatbot? A: A rule-based chatbot follows buttons, keywords and a fixed decision tree, so it fails when people phrase things their own way. An AI chatbot understands free text, keeps track of the conversation and answers from your content. We still use buttons and fixed flows inside an AI bot where precision matters, such as taking a payment. Q: Do we need a custom chatbot or a packaged chat agent? A: If you need common support or WhatsApp sales jobs on standard tools, our packaged Support Agent or WhatsApp Agent goes live in about two weeks. Choose a custom chatbot when it must work with unusual systems, serve staff rather than customers, live inside your own product or meet strict data rules."},{"id":"k115","title":"AI chatbot development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Q: How do you stop the chatbot from making things up? A: The bot only answers from the content you approve, and when that content does not cover a question it says so and offers a person. Before launch it must pass a test set built from your real conversations, and we review transcripts in the first weeks to close the gaps. Q: Can the chatbot speak Arabic and Urdu? A: Yes. It understands and replies in Arabic, Urdu, English and other major languages, including Roman Urdu and messages that switch language halfway. It answers in the customer's language by default, and we test each language on real phrasing from your market before launch."},{"id":"k116","title":"AI chatbot development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Q: Can it run on WhatsApp and Instagram? A: Yes, through the WhatsApp Business Platform and Meta's messaging APIs. Meta has rules on when a business can message first and which templates it can use, and we build the bot around them. We also help you set up and verify the business account if you do not have one yet. Q: Can a chatbot be used with patient data under HIPAA? A: It can, with the right setup. We deploy on providers that sign a BAA, keep data in your chosen region, encrypt it, limit what the bot can see and log every access. We document the data flow so your compliance lead can review it and sign off."},{"id":"k117","title":"AI chatbot development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Q: What happens when the bot cannot help? A: It hands the conversation to a person in your help desk, shared inbox or WhatsApp team inbox, with the transcript and a one-line summary. Outside working hours it collects contact details and tells the customer when to expect a reply."},{"id":"k118","title":"Services: AI voice agents","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Price: From $1,500. Visionbotix builds AI voice agents that answer and make phone calls for clinics, service businesses, sales and support teams. They hold natural conversations, book into your calendar, update your CRM, transfer to a person on your rules and tell callers they are speaking to an AI. Packaged receptionists go live in about two weeks; custom voice agents are fixed price."},{"id":"k119","title":"AI voice agents: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Q: What is an AI voice agent? A: It is software that answers or makes phone calls and talks like a person. Speech recognition turns the caller's words into text, a language model decides what to say and do, and a synthetic voice replies, while connections to your calendar and CRM let it book, look up and update records during the call. Q: Do callers have to be told they are talking to an AI? A: We build the disclosure in for every client, whatever the local rules say, because callers trust a clear answer more than a surprise. The greeting says it is an AI assistant, and asking for a person transfers the call or books a callback."},{"id":"k120","title":"AI voice agents: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Q: Can it make outbound calls? A: Yes, for reminders, confirmations, lead follow-up and qualification. In many countries, including the US and UK, automated or AI-voiced calls need prior consent and must respect calling hours and do-not-call lists. We build consent checks, calling windows and opt-outs into every campaign, but your legal team should confirm the rules for each market you call. Q: How natural does it sound? A: Close to a person on a good line. We pick a voice from ElevenLabs or another provider, tune how quickly it responds and let it handle interruptions and pauses. You hear recorded test calls before go-live and can change the voice or wording at any point."},{"id":"k121","title":"AI voice agents: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Q: Can it work with our existing phone system? A: Yes. You can forward your current number, use a new Twilio number or connect a SIP trunk to your PBX or contact center platform. The agent can transfer calls to extensions, queues or mobile numbers based on your rules. Q: Can it handle callers in different languages? A: Yes. The agent greets callers in your main language and switches when the caller does, across English, Arabic, Urdu and other major languages. We choose a voice per language and test each one with the phrasing and accents your callers actually use."},{"id":"k122","title":"AI voice agents: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Q: Are call recordings stored safely? A: Recording is optional and announced when it is on. Recordings and transcripts are encrypted, stored in the region you choose and deleted on your schedule, and for US healthcare we deploy on providers that sign a BAA."},{"id":"k123","title":"Services: AI consulting","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Price: From $490. Visionbotix offers AI consulting services for business leaders who want a clear AI plan. We start with a 1-week AI Opportunity Audit: we map your workflows, rank AI use cases by value and risk, check data readiness and recommend build, buy or wait in a written plan. The audit fee is credited in full against a build within 60 days."},{"id":"k124","title":"AI consulting: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Q: What does an AI consultant actually do? A: An AI consultant helps you decide where AI pays off and how to adopt it safely. That means mapping your workflows, ranking use cases, choosing between tools and custom builds, checking your data and setting rules for how staff use AI. Because we also build AI systems, our advice is grounded in what is practical to ship. Q: What is the AI Opportunity Audit? A: It is a fixed-scope, one-week engagement. We interview your team, map where AI could help, test the best ideas on your data and hand over a written plan with ranked use cases, build-vs-buy advice and governance steps. If you start a build with us within 60 days, the audit fee is credited in full."},{"id":"k125","title":"AI consulting: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Q: Do we have to build with you after the audit? A: No. The plan is yours to use with your own team, another vendor or an off-the-shelf tool. We write it so anyone can act on it, and the credit simply applies if you choose us within 60 days. Q: Is our data ready for AI? A: Often more than you think, because many useful projects start with documents, emails and tickets you already have. The data readiness review shows, per use case, what exists, what is missing or messy, and whether you are allowed to use it, so you know what to fix first."},{"id":"k126","title":"AI consulting: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Q: Do you help with AI governance and the EU AI Act? A: Yes. We draft an AI use policy, build a register of the AI systems you use, map each to its likely risk tier and set approval and human-oversight steps. This is practical awareness, not legal advice, and we flag where your counsel should review. Q: Should we build our own AI or buy a tool? A: Buy when the job is common and a vendor already does it well on acceptable data terms. Build when the work depends on your own process, systems or data, or when AI is part of what you sell. Most companies end up with a mix, and the audit says which applies to each use case."},{"id":"k127","title":"AI consulting: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Q: Can you train our team to use AI? A: Yes. We run practical workshops for leaders and staff built around their own tasks, covering safe use of AI tools, good prompting and how to spot work worth automating. Training can sit alongside your new AI use policy so people know what is allowed."},{"id":"k128","title":"Services: Custom software development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Price: From $5,000. Visionbotix builds custom software for businesses that have outgrown spreadsheets and off-the-shelf tools: internal tools, customer portals, ERP and CRM extensions, integrations and APIs, and modernized legacy systems. We can take over an existing codebase, add AI features where they save real time, and demo progress weekly. Projects are fixed price by milestone, and you own the code."},{"id":"k129","title":"Custom software development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Q: What is custom software development? A: It is software designed and built for your own processes, users and data, instead of a product you rent and adapt to. You decide what it does, it connects to the systems you already use, and you own the code outright. Q: Should we buy off-the-shelf software or build custom? A: Buy when a mainstream product fits most of your process and the gap is minor. Build when the gap is the part that makes your business different, when you are paying for several tools to fake one workflow, or when the tool cannot connect to your other systems. Often the right answer is both, with a custom layer on top of what you already own."},{"id":"k130","title":"Custom software development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Q: Can you take over a codebase another team built? A: Yes. We start with a short audit of the code, infrastructure and documentation, tell you plainly what is sound and what is risky, and then fix the urgent issues and keep shipping. You get a written report either way. Q: How do you modernize a legacy system without stopping the business? A: We replace it in slices. The new system runs alongside the old one, data syncs between them, and each module moves over only after it is tested against real records. Your team keeps working throughout, and there is always a way back until cutover."},{"id":"k131","title":"Custom software development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Q: Can you integrate with our ERP, CRM or accounting software? A: Usually, yes. If the system has an API, webhooks or a database we can reach, we can integrate with it. We check access and limits during discovery, before you commit to a fixed price. Q: How long does a custom software project take? A: A focused first release, such as an internal tool or a portal, is usually live in 8–14 weeks. Larger systems are planned in milestones that each deliver something your team can use, and you see a working demo every week."},{"id":"k132","title":"Custom software development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Q: Do we own the software and the code? A: Yes. The contract assigns 100% of the code and IP to you on payment, the repository lives in your account, and the documentation is written so any competent team can maintain it, with or without us."},{"id":"k133","title":"Services: Web app development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Price: From $3,000. Visionbotix designs and builds web apps for startups and growing businesses: dashboards, customer portals, marketplaces, e-commerce stores, progressive web apps and marketing sites. We use React, Next.js, Astro and Node or Laravel, and build for speed, accessibility and search from day one. You see a working demo every week, pay by milestone, and own the code."},{"id":"k134","title":"Web app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Q: What is the difference between a website and a web app? A: A website mostly shows information, such as pages about your company or products. A web app lets people do things, such as log in, order, book, upload or manage data. Many projects are both, and we build them on one stack so the marketing pages and the product share a design and a domain. Q: Which framework will you use? A: We choose for your product, not for habit. Next.js or Astro suit sites where search matters, React, Angular or Vue suit complex logged-in apps, and Node, NestJS or Laravel sit behind them. We explain the choice in the scope, and every option is mainstream enough that any good developer can pick it up."},{"id":"k135","title":"Web app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Q: Will the new site be good for SEO and AI search? A: Yes, we build for it from the start. Pages are fast, rendered on the server or pre-built, marked up with structured data and written so each page answers one question clearly. When you relaunch, we map and redirect old URLs so existing rankings carry over. Q: Should we build a progressive web app or a native mobile app? A: A progressive web app is a good first step when your users mainly need forms, browsing and notifications, because one codebase covers every device and there is no app store review. Choose a native or cross-platform app when you need deep device features, offline-heavy use or a store presence. We can start with a PWA and add mobile apps later on the same back end."},{"id":"k136","title":"Web app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Q: Can you redesign or rebuild our existing site without losing traffic? A: Yes. We audit what ranks and converts today, keep or improve those pages, set up redirects for every URL that changes and check search console after launch. Content and data move across before the switch, not after. Q: Can our team update content without a developer? A: Yes. We connect a headless CMS or an admin panel for pages, blog posts, products and media, with roles so editors cannot break the layout. We show your team how to use it before launch."},{"id":"k137","title":"Web app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Q: Who hosts the web app after launch? A: You choose. We deploy to your own Vercel, AWS, Google Cloud or Azure account, so the hosting bills and access are yours. We can keep it running for you on a monthly plan, or hand it over to your team."},{"id":"k138","title":"Services: Mobile app development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Price: From $8,000. Visionbotix builds iOS and Android apps for startups and businesses, in native Swift and Kotlin or cross-platform with React Native or Flutter. We handle design, offline mode, push, payments, AI features, the back end and store submission. Apps built by our team are live on the App Store and Google Play. Fixed price by milestone, and you own the code."},{"id":"k139","title":"Mobile app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Q: Do we need separate apps for iOS and Android? A: Usually not. React Native and Flutter let one team ship both from a single codebase, which keeps features in step and lowers the cost of every change. Native Swift and Kotlin make sense when the app leans hard on device features, heavy graphics or the latest platform APIs. Q: React Native or Flutter, which should we choose? A: Both are mature and both reach iOS and Android. React Native is the natural pick if you have a React web app or a JavaScript team, because code and skills carry over. Flutter suits highly custom, brand-led interfaces that must look identical on every phone. We recommend one in the scope and explain why."},{"id":"k140","title":"Mobile app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Q: Will you publish the app to the App Store and Google Play? A: Yes. We prepare the listings, screenshots, privacy labels and review notes, submit the builds and handle any reviewer questions. Store approval is Apple's and Google's decision, so we design to their guidelines from the start to avoid surprises. Q: Can the app work offline? A: Yes, when the product needs it. We store data on the device, queue changes while there is no signal and sync them safely when the connection returns, with clear rules for conflicts."},{"id":"k141","title":"Mobile app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Q: Can you add AI features to a mobile app? A: Yes. Common examples are document and photo scanning, voice input, translation, smart search and in-app assistants. Some run on the device for speed and privacy, others call a model in the cloud, and we set cost limits and guardrails either way. Q: Can you take over or fix an app another developer built? A: Yes. We review the code, dependencies, crash reports and store status, tell you plainly what to keep and what to rebuild, and then fix the urgent issues first. You get a written report before you commit to anything larger."},{"id":"k142","title":"Mobile app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Q: Who owns the app, the code and the store listings? A: You do. The App Store and Google Play accounts, signing keys and repository are set up in your name, and the contract assigns 100% of the code and IP to you on payment."},{"id":"k143","title":"Services: SaaS and MVP development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Price: From $12,000. Visionbotix builds SaaS products and MVPs for founders and product teams. We scope the smallest launchable version, then build it with sign-in, roles, Stripe billing, an admin panel, analytics and AI features, on a multi-tenant base that can scale. You get a demo every week, a fixed price per milestone, an NDA from the first call, and all the code."},{"id":"k144","title":"SaaS and MVP development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Q: What is an MVP, and what should ours include? A: An MVP is the smallest version of your product that real users can use and pay for, so you learn what works before building more. Ours usually include one core journey done well, sign-in, basic admin and, for SaaS, billing. Everything else goes on a later list that real usage will reorder. Q: How is this different from your AI MVP Sprint? A: The AI MVP Sprint is a packaged, fixed-scope offer that takes an AI-native idea to a working product in 6–8 weeks. This service covers any SaaS or MVP, with or without AI, and the path after launch, such as multi-tenant scale, larger billing models and enterprise features."},{"id":"k145","title":"SaaS and MVP development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Will we have to rebuild the MVP later? A: Not if it is built right. We cut features, not foundations, so the MVP already has a clean data model, tenant separation, tests and mainstream frameworks. Growing it means adding modules, not starting again. Q: We are non-technical founders. Can you still work with us? A: Yes. You do not need to know the technology to make good product decisions. You get one named lead who explains choices in plain words, a weekly demo you can click through, and a written scope so you always know what is being built and why."},{"id":"k146","title":"SaaS and MVP development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Can you add AI features to our SaaS? A: Yes. Common examples are assistants that know a customer's own data, document extraction, smart search, summaries and agents that complete tasks. We keep each customer's data separate, set usage limits per account and test the features against real cases before launch. Q: What happens after the MVP launches? A: You get 30 days of support for fixes and tuning. After that you can continue with us on a monthly plan or a dedicated team, or take the code to your own developers, since you own the repository and the documentation."},{"id":"k147","title":"SaaS and MVP development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Do we own the code and the IP? A: Yes. The contract assigns 100% of the code and IP to you on payment, and the repository, cloud accounts and Stripe account are in your name from day one, which matters when you raise money."},{"id":"k148","title":"Services: UI/UX design","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Price: From $1,500. Visionbotix offers UI/UX design for web apps, mobile apps and SaaS products: discovery, UX research, wireframes, clickable Figma prototypes, design systems and accessible interfaces to WCAG AA. We also design AI features so users can see what an agent did and approve it. Start with a design sprint for one product flow, then build it with us or any developer."},{"id":"k149","title":"UI/UX design: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Q: What is the difference between UI and UX design? A: UX design is how the product works, such as the steps a user takes, what they see first and how they recover from mistakes. UI design is how it looks, such as layout, type, color and components. You need both, and we do both in one team. Q: What is a design sprint for one product flow? A: It is a short, fixed-scope engagement that takes one important journey, such as onboarding, checkout or an AI approval flow, from research to a tested, clickable prototype. It is the fastest way to fix a weak flow or to see how we work before a larger project."},{"id":"k150","title":"UI/UX design: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Q: Do you only design, or can you build it too? A: Both. You can take the Figma files and the component library to your own developers, or we can build the product with our web and mobile teams, so nothing is lost between design and code. Q: Can you redesign our product without confusing existing users? A: Yes. We find the screens that cause the most friction, redesign those first and roll changes out in stages, often behind a toggle for early users. Familiar patterns stay where they work."},{"id":"k151","title":"UI/UX design: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Q: How do you design for AI features and agents? A: We make the AI's work visible. Users see what the agent is doing, which sources it used and what it plans to change, and anything risky waits for their approval. We also design how users correct the AI, because trust comes from being able to undo. Q: Will the design be accessible? A: Yes. We design to WCAG AA by default, covering contrast, focus states, keyboard paths, touch target sizes and screen reader labels, and we note these in the handoff so they survive the build."},{"id":"k152","title":"UI/UX design: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Q: Do we own the design files? A: Yes. The Figma files, components, icons made for you and all design IP are yours on payment, in your own Figma workspace if you prefer."},{"id":"k153","title":"Services: Cloud and DevOps","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Price: From $1,500. Visionbotix sets up and runs cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, Google Cloud and Vercel. We build CI/CD pipelines, write the infrastructure as code in Terraform, containerize apps with Docker and Kubernetes, add monitoring and review your cloud bill. We also host private open models on GPUs for AI workloads. Fixed price, and you own every line."},{"id":"k154","title":"Cloud and DevOps: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Q: What do cloud and DevOps services include? A: They cover how your software is hosted, built, released and watched in production. In practice that means a cloud architecture, a CI/CD pipeline, infrastructure as code, containers, monitoring and alerts, and regular cost reviews. You can take one piece, such as a pipeline, or the whole setup. Q: Which cloud should we use? A: It depends on your team, your customers and your data rules more than on features. Vercel or a similar managed platform suits most web products early on, AWS, Azure and Google Cloud suit larger or regulated workloads, and some enterprise buyers require a specific one. We recommend one in writing after the first review."},{"id":"k155","title":"Cloud and DevOps: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Q: Do we really need Kubernetes? A: Often not. Kubernetes pays off when you run many services, need fine control over scaling or must run the same stack across clouds and on-premises. For a single app or a small team, a managed platform or containers on simpler cloud services cost less to run and are easier to hire for. Q: Can you reduce our cloud bill? A: Usually, yes. We review every line of the bill, remove idle resources, right-size servers and databases, and move steady workloads to reserved or committed pricing. You get a ranked list of changes with the effort each one takes, and we make the ones you approve."},{"id":"k156","title":"Cloud and DevOps: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Q: Can you host an open-source LLM privately for us? A: Yes. We deploy open models such as Llama, Mistral or DeepSeek on GPU servers in your cloud account or on your own hardware, with an API your apps can call, access controls and usage monitoring. Prompts and data stay inside your network. Q: Will we be locked in to you? A: No. Everything is written as Terraform and pipeline code in your repository, in your cloud accounts, with runbooks your team can follow. You own 100% of the code and IP, and you can run it with or without us."},{"id":"k157","title":"Cloud and DevOps: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Q: Do you offer ongoing DevOps support? A: Yes. After 30 days of included support you can move to a monthly plan in which we watch alerts, apply updates, review costs and handle changes. Or we train your team and step back."},{"id":"k158","title":"Services: Dedicated teams","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Price: From $2,200/mo. Visionbotix gives you full-time AI and ML engineers, full-stack and mobile developers, UI/UX designers and QA engineers who work only on your product. They join your Slack, Jira and GitHub, follow your sprints, overlap your working hours and report through one named lead. You scale the team up or down as the roadmap changes, and you own all the code."},{"id":"k159","title":"Dedicated teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Q: What is a dedicated development team? A: It is a group of full-time engineers and designers who work only on your product, inside your tools and sprints. You set the priorities day to day, and we handle hiring, payroll, equipment and management through one named lead. Q: How is this different from hiring freelancers? A: Freelancers usually split their time across clients and leave when the contract ends. Our engineers are full time on your product, work as one team, and are backed by a company that stays responsible for delivery and continuity."},{"id":"k160","title":"Dedicated teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Q: Which time zones do you cover? A: Our engineers work hours that overlap the US, UK, Europe, the Gulf and Australia. We agree the overlap window for each role before the team starts, so standups and reviews happen live. Q: Can we interview the developers first? A: Yes. We propose engineers who match the brief, you interview them, and only the people you approve join your team."},{"id":"k161","title":"Dedicated teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Q: Can we scale the team up or down? A: Yes. You can add roles as the roadmap grows or reduce the team when a phase ends, with the notice period agreed in the contract. The named lead keeps knowledge in your repository and docs, so changes do not set the work back. Q: Who owns the code and IP? A: You do. The contract assigns 100% of the code and IP to you, all work happens in your repository, and we sign an NDA on request before you share anything."},{"id":"k162","title":"Dedicated teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Q: Can a dedicated team build AI features? A: Yes. Our AI and ML engineers build agents, RAG systems, evals and model integrations with Claude, GPT, Gemini and open models, and they work alongside your existing developers so the skills stay with your team."},{"id":"k163","title":"Services: Computer vision","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Price: From $10,000. Visionbotix builds custom computer vision systems that detect objects, inspect products for defects, read text, recognize authorized people and count footfall. We train models on your own images and run them on your cameras, on edge devices such as NVIDIA Jetson and Raspberry Pi, or in your cloud. Prototypes are fixed price, and you own the model and code."},{"id":"k164","title":"Computer vision: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Q: What can computer vision do for my business? A: It turns camera images into decisions or data. Common uses are spotting defective parts on a line, reading labels and meters, controlling entry, counting people or stock, and flagging safety risks. If a person can see it consistently in an image, a model can usually be trained to see it too. Q: How many images do we need to train a model? A: It depends on how varied your product and conditions are. Many projects start with a few hundred labeled images per class and grow from there, and we tell you after the first week whether your data is enough. We can also help you capture and label it."},{"id":"k165","title":"Computer vision: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Q: Can the system run without the cloud? A: Yes. We deploy models on edge devices such as NVIDIA Jetson, Raspberry Pi or an industrial PC next to the camera, so images are processed on site and the system keeps working offline. Only alerts or counts need to leave the device, if anything does. Q: Can you use our existing cameras? A: Often, yes. Most IP cameras that provide a standard video stream work. If the resolution, angle or lighting is not good enough for the task, we recommend specific changes before training starts rather than after."},{"id":"k166","title":"Computer vision: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Q: How do you handle privacy for face recognition? A: We build face recognition only where people have consented, with a clear enrollment step, encrypted storage of face templates and retention rules you approve. For counting and occupancy we use detection without identity, so nobody is recognized. Q: How accurate will the model be? A: We agree the target with you before training, measure it on images the model has never seen, and report the results honestly. Accuracy depends on your data and conditions, so the pilot on real cameras is where we prove it before a full rollout."},{"id":"k167","title":"Computer vision: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Q: Do you have your own vision products? A: Yes. We built and run Smart Livestock, an AI platform for dairy and livestock farms, and Vision AI cameras. The same team builds custom vision systems for clients."},{"id":"k168","title":"Services: IoT and embedded","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Price: From $10,000. Visionbotix designs and builds connected devices end to end: sensor networks, firmware, embedded Linux, FPGA logic, edge AI and ROS robots, connected over MQTT, LoRa, BLE or cellular to dashboards that manage the whole fleet. We take you from a working prototype to a field pilot in milestones at a fixed price, and you own the designs and code."},{"id":"k169","title":"IoT and embedded: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Q: What do IoT development services cover? A: Everything needed to put a connected device in the field. That includes choosing sensors and boards, writing the firmware, setting up connectivity, building the backend that stores the data and the dashboard or app people use. We can take on the whole system or one layer of it. Q: Can you take us from an idea to a working prototype? A: Yes. We start with a short feasibility phase to choose components and test the riskiest assumptions, then build a working bench prototype with firmware, data and a first dashboard. A field pilot follows once the prototype proves the idea."},{"id":"k170","title":"IoT and embedded: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Q: Which connectivity should we use? A: It depends on range, power and how much data each device sends. LoRa suits small readings over long distances on battery, BLE suits short range and phones, Wi-Fi suits buildings with power, and cellular suits mobile or remote assets. MQTT usually carries the messages once the link is chosen. Q: Do you design FPGA logic? A: Yes. We design FPGA logic for high-speed processing, encryption and real-time control, and our own VX-1 IP Encryptor runs its encryption entirely in FPGA hardware. FPGA work suits problems where software on a processor is too slow or too exposed."},{"id":"k171","title":"IoT and embedded: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Q: Can the devices run AI on the edge? A: Yes. We run vision and anomaly-detection models on NVIDIA Jetson, Raspberry Pi and capable microcontrollers, so decisions happen next to the sensor and the device keeps working when the network drops. Q: Do you manufacture the hardware? A: We design and build prototypes and pilot batches, and we prepare the designs and documentation for a manufacturer of your choice to produce at volume. We can stay involved for testing and firmware updates during that handover."},{"id":"k172","title":"IoT and embedded: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Q: How long does a hardware project take? A: A working prototype usually takes six to ten weeks and a field pilot three to six months, depending on how custom the hardware is. Hardware takes longer than software because parts, enclosures and field testing add steps, so we plan it in milestones you can see."},{"id":"k173","title":"Services: Cybersecurity","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Price: From $2,500. Visionbotix secures AI systems and sensitive networks. We red-team LLM apps and agents for prompt injection, data leakage and tool misuse, review the architecture of the software we build, and make our own security products: the VX-1 hardware IP encryptor, ThreatIQ for air-gapped networks and a Cyber Range for team training and device testing. NDA on request from the first call."},{"id":"k174","title":"Cybersecurity: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Q: What cybersecurity services do you offer? A: We focus on two areas. For AI systems, we red-team LLM apps and agents and review the architecture of the software we build. For sensitive networks, we offer our own products, the VX-1 IP Encryptor, ThreatIQ and the Cyber Range, which are deployed and supported by our team. Q: What is LLM red teaming? A: It is a structured attempt to make your AI app misbehave the way a real attacker would. We try to override its instructions, extract its system prompt, reach other users' data and misuse the tools it can call, then document what worked and how to fix it."},{"id":"k175","title":"Cybersecurity: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Q: Does this replace a traditional penetration test? A: No. A traditional pen test covers your network, servers and web application. LLM red teaming covers the AI layer that those tests were not designed for, such as prompt injection and tool misuse. Most products with AI features need both. Q: Can you secure an AI agent that has access to our systems? A: Yes. We review every tool the agent can call, cut its permissions to what the job needs, add approval steps for risky actions and test whether it can be talked into misusing them. We can also build a secure MCP server so the agent reaches your systems through one controlled gateway."},{"id":"k176","title":"Cybersecurity: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Q: What is the VX-1 IP Encryptor? A: It is our hardware network encryptor. It encrypts IP traffic between sites with AES-256 in counter mode on dedicated FPGA hardware, with no operating system to attack. It works transparently on Layer 2 and Layer 3 links, including satellite connections, and its output was checked against the NIST FIPS 197 reference vectors. Q: How does ThreatIQ protect an air-gapped network? A: ThreatIQ runs as a dedicated appliance inside the isolated network with lightweight clients on each endpoint. It assesses vulnerabilities across malware, software, operating systems, web apps, network traffic and services, watches for unusual insider behavior and benchmarks configurations against recognized hardening baselines such as the CIS Benchmarks, all without an internet connection."},{"id":"k177","title":"Cybersecurity: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Q: Who is the Cyber Range for? A: It is for security teams that need to practice attack and defense safely, and for organizations that want to test network and security devices before buying them. It runs red team and blue team exercises on realistic simulated traffic and benchmarks devices against standards such as RFC 2544 and RFC 3511, with training for your operators. Q: Is our information kept confidential? A: Yes. We sign an NDA on request before the first technical conversation, test in environments you approve and share findings only with the people you name. Our security products are built for defense, government and enterprise environments where discretion is the norm."},{"id":"k178","title":"Industries: AI agents for healthcare providers","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/healthcare/","text":"Visionbotix sets up AI agents for healthcare providers: a receptionist that answers patient calls 24/7, a booking agent that confirms and reschedules appointments, a document agent that reads referrals and intake forms, and a reputation agent that asks for reviews. They follow your triage rules, never give clinical advice and go live in two to four weeks. Rules we design around: HIPAA (US), UK GDPR and DPA 2018 (UK), GDPR (EU), TCPA and PECR (US · UK). Clinic Front Desk bundle from $3,000 + $699/mo."},{"id":"k179","title":"AI agents for healthcare providers: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/healthcare/","text":"Q: Can an AI receptionist give medical advice? A: No. It answers from facts you approve, such as hours, services, insurance and preparation instructions, and follows your triage protocol. Calls that match your red flags go to a clinician or get the emergency message you approve, and it never suggests a diagnosis or treatment. Q: Can we use AI agents in a HIPAA-regulated practice? A: Yes, when they are set up for it. We use providers that sign a Business Associate Agreement, keep patient data out of model training, encrypt it and limit what each agent can see. HIPAA compliance stays your organization's responsibility, so we document the setup for your privacy officer."},{"id":"k180","title":"AI agents for healthcare providers: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/healthcare/","text":"Q: Will it work with our EHR or practice management system? A: The agents read and write appointments in systems such as Cliniko and in Google or Microsoft calendars. For EHRs such as athenahealth or eClinicalWorks we use the vendor's API or another secure integration route, and we confirm which one on the first call, before you pay anything. Q: How does intake document processing work? A: Referral letters, intake forms and insurance cards are read from PDFs, scans or photos, and the fields you need are extracted and checked for gaps. Anything uncertain goes to a review screen with the document side by side, and nothing reaches the patient record until a staff member confirms it."},{"id":"k181","title":"AI agents for healthcare providers: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/healthcare/","text":"Q: Does it work for therapy clinics, labs and home care? A: Yes, with rules set for each. Therapy clinics book recurring sessions with the same clinician, labs send preparation instructions and answer walk-in questions, and home care agencies take inquiries from families and route care questions to a coordinator. Q: Will patients know they are talking to an AI? A: Yes. The greeting says it is the clinic's AI assistant, and a patient can ask for a person at any time to be transferred or called back."},{"id":"k182","title":"AI agents for healthcare providers: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/healthcare/","text":"Q: How long does it take to go live? A: The receptionist goes live in about two weeks; the document agent takes two to four weeks because it is set up on your own forms. You can start with after-hours and overflow calls only, review the first week of transcripts with us, and then let the agents take on reminders, intake and reviews."},{"id":"k183","title":"Industries: AI agents for dental clinics","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/dental-clinics/","text":"Visionbotix sets up AI agents for dental clinics: a receptionist that answers every call 24/7, a booking agent that fills cancelled slots and sends reminders, and a reputation agent that asks happy patients for reviews. They connect to your practice software, follow your own triage rules and go live in about two weeks. Rules we design around: HIPAA (US), UK GDPR and DPA 2018 (UK), Australian Privacy Act (Australia), TCPA and PECR (US · UK). Clinic Front Desk bundle from $3,000 + $699/mo."},{"id":"k184","title":"AI agents for dental clinics: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/dental-clinics/","text":"Q: Can an AI receptionist handle dental emergencies? A: It follows the triage rules you give it. Calls about pain, swelling, bleeding or a knocked-out tooth are booked into your emergency slots or transferred to the on-call dentist straight away, with a short summary. It never tells a patient what treatment they need. Q: Will it work with our practice management software? A: The agents read and write appointments in common dental systems such as Open Dental, Dentally, Cliniko and Curve Dental, and in Google or Microsoft calendars. For other systems we use the vendor's API or a secure integration route; we confirm which one on the first call, before you pay anything."},{"id":"k185","title":"AI agents for dental clinics: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/dental-clinics/","text":"Q: Can we use it in a HIPAA-regulated practice? A: Yes, when it is set up for it. We use providers that sign a Business Associate Agreement, keep patient data out of model training, encrypt it and limit what the agent can see. HIPAA compliance stays your practice's responsibility, so we document the setup for your privacy officer. Q: Will patients know they are talking to an AI? A: Yes. The greeting says it is the practice's AI assistant, and a patient can ask for a person at any time to be transferred or called back. Patients get a straight answer instead of a voice pretending to be human."},{"id":"k186","title":"AI agents for dental clinics: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/dental-clinics/","text":"Q: Does it replace our front desk team? A: No. It takes the repetitive calls, the after-hours calls and the reminders, so your team can look after the patients in front of them. Anything sensitive, unusual or clinical goes to a person. Q: How long does it take to go live? A: About two weeks. You can start with after-hours and overflow calls only, review the first week of transcripts with us, and then let the agent answer more."},{"id":"k187","title":"Industries: AI agents for real estate agencies","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/real-estate/","text":"Visionbotix sets up AI agents for real estate agencies: a lead agent that replies to portal and ad inquiries in seconds and books viewings, a WhatsApp agent for buyers and tenants, a receptionist for calls while agents are out, and an SDR agent for landlord and investor outreach. They connect to your CRM and go live in about two weeks. Rules we design around: Fair Housing Act (US), TCPA and Do Not Call (US), UK GDPR and PECR (UK), UAE PDPL (UAE). Real Estate Lead Desk bundle from $4,500 + $899/mo."},{"id":"k188","title":"AI agents for real estate agencies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/real-estate/","text":"Q: Will it work with our CRM and the property portals? A: In most setups, yes. Portal leads usually reach you by email or API, and the agent picks them up from there and logs every conversation in Follow Up Boss, HubSpot, Salesforce, Zoho CRM or another CRM with an API. We confirm the route for your stack on the first call, before you pay anything. Q: Can an AI qualify leads without breaking fair housing rules? A: Yes, if the questions are written for it. The agent asks only about budget, timing, area, property needs and financing stage, and it never asks about or comments on protected characteristics or who lives in a neighborhood. We review the qualifying script with you before launch, and fair housing compliance stays your brokerage's responsibility."},{"id":"k189","title":"AI agents for real estate agencies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/real-estate/","text":"Q: What happens when a buyer wants to make an offer? A: The agent does not negotiate. It thanks the buyer, says the listing agent will be in touch, and passes the conversation to the agent on duty with a summary of the property, the buyer's position and what they asked. Q: Does it work on WhatsApp and in Arabic? A: Yes. The WhatsApp agent runs on the official WhatsApp Business Platform and replies in English, Arabic and other languages your buyers use. Buyers and tenants message in the language they prefer, and the agent books the viewing in the same chat."},{"id":"k190","title":"AI agents for real estate agencies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/real-estate/","text":"Q: Will buyers know they are talking to an AI? A: Yes. The first message or greeting says it is your agency's AI assistant, and anyone can ask for a person at any time. Buyers and tenants get a straight answer instead of a bot pretending to be an agent. Q: Does it replace our agents or our ISA? A: No. It takes the first reply, the qualifying questions, the viewing admin and the long follow-up, so your agents spend their time on viewings, valuations and negotiations. You can start with nights and weekends only, then widen what it handles."},{"id":"k191","title":"AI agents for real estate agencies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/real-estate/","text":"Q: How long does it take to go live? A: About two weeks. We map your lead sources and booking rules, write the conversations with you, connect your CRM and calendars, and run test leads through every path before the first real one arrives."},{"id":"k192","title":"Industries: AI agents for online stores","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/ecommerce/","text":"Visionbotix sets up AI agents for online stores: a support agent for order and return questions on chat and email, a WhatsApp agent that answers shoppers and recovers carts, a reputation agent that asks every buyer for a review, and an ads agent that checks your campaigns daily. They connect to your store and go live in about two weeks. Rules we design around: PCI DSS (Global), GDPR and UK GDPR (EU · UK), CCPA and CPRA (US · California), Marketing consent (Global · US · UK), EU and UK distance selling rules (EU · UK). E-commerce Support Desk bundle from $3,900 + $799/mo."},{"id":"k193","title":"AI agents for online stores: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/ecommerce/","text":"Q: Does it work with Shopify, WooCommerce and our help desk? A: Yes. The agents read orders, stock and customers from Shopify, WooCommerce or Magento, and work inside help desks such as Gorgias and Zendesk so your team sees every conversation. For other platforms we use the vendor's API and confirm the route on the first call. Q: Can the AI issue refunds on its own? A: No. It checks the order against your returns policy, starts the return and prepares the refund, then passes it to staff to approve. No money moves without a person signing off."},{"id":"k194","title":"AI agents for online stores: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/ecommerce/","text":"Q: Will WhatsApp messages get our number banned? A: The WhatsApp agent runs on the official WhatsApp Business Platform, not unofficial tools. It replies freely inside the 24-hour customer service window, uses Meta-approved templates outside it, and sends marketing messages only to shoppers who opted in. Q: Is it allowed to ask customers for reviews? A: Yes, when it is done fairly. The reputation agent asks every customer, not only the happy ones, offers no incentives and never writes reviews, in line with Google and Trustpilot policies and FTC rules on reviews. Replies to negative reviews wait for your approval."},{"id":"k195","title":"AI agents for online stores: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/ecommerce/","text":"Q: Could the ads agent overspend our budget? A: No. It cannot create campaigns, raise your total budget or change billing. Small pauses happen within the thresholds you set, bigger changes become proposals for approval, and a pause switch puts it into report-only mode at once. Q: Which languages does it handle? A: The agents reply in the language the customer writes in, including English, Arabic, Urdu and other major languages. Replies still come only from your catalog and policies, whatever the language."},{"id":"k196","title":"AI agents for online stores: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/ecommerce/","text":"Q: How long does it take to go live? A: About two weeks. We review a sample of your tickets and chats, load your catalog and policies, connect your store and channels, and test every common question before customers see it."},{"id":"k197","title":"Industries: AI agents for law firms","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/legal/","text":"Visionbotix sets up AI agents for law firms: a receptionist that answers every inquiry and collects intake details, a document agent that extracts key terms, a private knowledge assistant that answers from your precedents, and a booking agent that schedules consultations once conflicts are cleared. They never give legal advice and go live in two to four weeks. Rules we design around: ABA Model Rule 1.6 (US), ABA Model Rule 1.18 (US), SRA Standards and Regulations (England and Wales), GDPR and UK GDPR (UK · EU). Receptionist Agent from $1,500 + $349/mo."},{"id":"k198","title":"AI agents for law firms: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/legal/","text":"Q: Will the AI give legal advice to callers? A: No. It answers practical questions from facts you approve, such as practice areas, office hours and what to bring to a consultation. Questions about the merits of a case, deadlines or likely outcomes go to a lawyer or the intake team. Q: How does it handle conflict checks? A: The receptionist collects party names, the matter type and key dates in a structured intake record. Your team, or the conflict search in your practice management system, runs the check, and the booking agent offers a consultation only after the intake is marked clear."},{"id":"k199","title":"AI agents for law firms: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/legal/","text":"Q: Is our client data used to train AI models? A: No. Documents and intake data stay in your chosen region and tenant and are never used for training, and the knowledge assistant can run in your own cloud or on-premise with an open-weight model. Professional conduct duties stay with the firm, so we document the setup for your risk and compliance lead. Q: Will it work with Clio or our document management system? A: The agents connect to common tools such as Clio, SharePoint, Microsoft 365 and calendar systems. For other practice and document management systems we use the vendor's API or another secure route, and we confirm which one on the first call."},{"id":"k200","title":"AI agents for law firms: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/legal/","text":"Q: Have you built AI for the legal sector before? A: Yes. We built and run Wakeel, an AI lawyer-matching platform in Pakistan where people describe a legal problem in Urdu or English, by text or voice, and are matched with verified advocates. The same intake and matching work goes into the agents we set up for firms. Q: Will callers know they are talking to an AI? A: Yes. The greeting says it is the firm's AI assistant, and a caller can ask for a person at any time to be transferred or called back."},{"id":"k201","title":"AI agents for law firms: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/legal/","text":"Q: How long does it take to go live? A: The receptionist goes live in about two weeks; the document and knowledge agents take two to four weeks because they are set up on your own files. You can start with after-hours intake only, review the first week of transcripts with us, and then add document extraction and precedent search."},{"id":"k202","title":"Industries: AI agents for financial services firms","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/finance/","text":"Visionbotix sets up AI agents for financial services firms: a document agent that reads KYC, loan and claims files, a knowledge assistant that answers from your policies with citations, a support agent for customer questions, and a security audit that red-teams the setup before launch. People keep every decision, and the agents go live in two to four weeks. Rules we design around: GLBA (US), PCI DSS (Global), GDPR and UK GDPR (EU · UK), AML and KYC rules (Global), EU AI Act (EU). Document Agent from $3,000 + $399/mo."},{"id":"k203","title":"AI agents for financial services firms: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/finance/","text":"Q: Will the AI make lending, underwriting or claims decisions? A: No. The agents read documents, check them against your rules, answer questions and flag what needs attention. Every credit, underwriting, claims and onboarding decision is made by a named person, and the audit log shows who made it. Q: Can it run in our own cloud? A: Yes. The document agent and knowledge assistant can be deployed in your private cloud on AWS, Azure or Google Cloud, or on-premise with an open-weight model, so documents never leave your environment. Data is never used to train models."},{"id":"k204","title":"AI agents for financial services firms: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/finance/","text":"Q: How do you stop it leaking one customer's data to another? A: The knowledge assistant checks document permissions through your identity provider at question time, sensitive numbers are masked before they reach the model, and each agent can reach only the systems and actions you approve. The security audit then tries to break exactly these controls before launch. Q: Will this satisfy our regulators and auditors? A: We do not certify anything on your behalf, and regulatory compliance stays your firm's responsibility. What we give you is the evidence reviewers ask for, such as a written description of the setup, data flows, access rules, a full audit log and a dated security testing report."},{"id":"k205","title":"AI agents for financial services firms: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/finance/","text":"Q: Can it give financial advice to customers? A: No. The support agent answers factual questions about your products and processes from approved content. Requests for advice, recommendations, complaints and anything about a customer's personal circumstances go straight to a person. Q: What does the security audit test? A: Prompt injection through the chat and through documents the agents read, jailbreaks, data leakage between customers, and whether any tool the agent can call could be misused. Testing runs against staging under signed rules of engagement, and findings come with fixes and a retest."},{"id":"k206","title":"AI agents for financial services firms: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/finance/","text":"Q: How long does it take to go live? A: Two to four weeks for the document agent and knowledge assistant, depending on the document types and sources involved, with the security audit report in about two weeks. You can start with one process, such as KYC intake, and add more after the first review."},{"id":"k207","title":"Industries: AI agents for logistics companies","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/logistics/","text":"Visionbotix sets up AI agents for logistics companies: a document agent that reads bills of lading, invoices and delivery notes, a support agent that answers tracking questions, a workflow agent that moves data between your TMS and ERP, and a knowledge assistant for SOPs and customer rules. They work alongside your team and go live in two to four weeks. Rules we design around: GDPR and UK GDPR (EU · UK), Customs record keeping (Global), Tax and invoice records (Global), Rate and contract confidentiality (Global). Document Agent from $3,000 + $399/mo."},{"id":"k208","title":"AI agents for logistics companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/logistics/","text":"Q: Can it read bills of lading from every carrier? A: It reads PDFs, scans, photos and email attachments in many layouts and languages, without a template per carrier. Each field gets a confidence check, and anything uncertain goes to a review screen with the document side by side. Q: Does it work with CargoWise or our own TMS? A: We connect through your system's API or another secure integration route, with read-only access by default. Writes, such as creating a draft job, are limited to the actions you approve. We confirm the route for your stack on the first call, before you pay anything."},{"id":"k209","title":"AI agents for logistics companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/logistics/","text":"Q: Will the AI file customs declarations? A: No. The document agent extracts and checks the data from commercial invoices, packing lists and other documents, and your licensed staff review and file the declaration. Nothing is submitted to a customs authority by the agent. Q: Can our customers track shipments through it? A: Yes. The support agent answers on web chat, email or WhatsApp with the status from your TMS or carrier, and passes delays, damage claims and anything unusual to your ops team with a summary."},{"id":"k210","title":"AI agents for logistics companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/logistics/","text":"Q: What about poor scans and handwritten PODs? A: Scans and phone photos are read like any other document. If a signature, stamp or handwritten note cannot be read with confidence, the document goes to a person instead of being posted. Q: Is our rate and customer data safe? A: Data is encrypted in transit and at rest, kept in the region you choose and never used to train models. For sensitive contracts we can deploy in your own cloud or on-premise, and every read and change is in the audit log."},{"id":"k211","title":"AI agents for logistics companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/logistics/","text":"Q: How long does it take to go live? A: Two to four weeks, depending on how many document types and systems are involved. You can start with one document type or one inbox, review the first weeks of exceptions with us, and then add more."},{"id":"k212","title":"Industries: AI agents for schools and training providers","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/education/","text":"Visionbotix sets up AI agents for schools and training providers: a support agent that answers applicants and students on your website, a WhatsApp agent for parents who prefer messaging, a booking agent for tours and open days, and a knowledge assistant that finds policies for staff. They never make admissions decisions and go live in two to four weeks. Rules we design around: FERPA (US), COPPA (US), UK GDPR and Children's Code (UK), Keeping Children Safe in Education (England). Support Agent from $2,500 + $449/mo."},{"id":"k213","title":"AI agents for schools and training providers: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/education/","text":"Q: Does the AI make admissions or grading decisions? A: No. It answers questions, collects inquiry details and books visits. Admissions, grading, scholarships and discipline stay with your staff, and the agents only pass information to them. Q: How are safeguarding concerns handled? A: You name the designated person and the words and topics that count as a concern. Any message that matches is passed to that person at once with the full conversation, and the agent replies only with the message you approve."},{"id":"k214","title":"AI agents for schools and training providers: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/education/","text":"Q: Is student data safe, and is it used to train AI models? A: Student data is encrypted, kept in the region you choose and never used for training. Each agent reads only the records its task needs, and every lookup is in the audit log. FERPA, COPPA and UK GDPR compliance stay with your institution, so we document the setup for your data protection lead. Q: Will it work with our student information system or LMS? A: The agents connect to help desks such as Zendesk, to Microsoft Teams, Google Workspace and WhatsApp, and to common CRMs. For student information systems and learning platforms such as PowerSchool or Canvas, we use the vendor's API and confirm the route on the first call."},{"id":"k215","title":"AI agents for schools and training providers: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/education/","text":"Q: Can it answer families in other languages? A: The WhatsApp agent replies in the language a parent writes in, including Arabic and Urdu, and the knowledge assistant works in English, Arabic and other major languages. We test each language you need before launch. Q: Will students and parents know they are talking to an AI? A: Yes. The agent introduces itself as the school's AI assistant, and anyone can ask for a person at any time."},{"id":"k216","title":"AI agents for schools and training providers: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/education/","text":"Q: How long does it take to go live? A: The first agent goes live in about two weeks; the knowledge assistant takes two to four weeks because it indexes your documents. You can start with admissions questions before an intake season, review the first weeks of conversations with us, and then add student support and staff search."},{"id":"k217","title":"Industries: AI agents for hotels and restaurants","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/hospitality/","text":"Visionbotix sets up AI agents for hotels and restaurants: a WhatsApp agent that answers guests and takes booking requests, a receptionist that picks up every call, a reputation agent that replies to reviews and a social media agent that keeps your accounts active. They never take card numbers, follow your house rules and go live in about two weeks. Rules we design around: PCI DSS (Global), GDPR and UK GDPR (UK · EU), Marketing consent (US · UK · EU), Food allergen information (UK · EU). WhatsApp Agent from $1,500 + $299/mo."},{"id":"k218","title":"AI agents for hotels and restaurants: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/hospitality/","text":"Q: Can the agent book rooms straight into our property management system? A: Table requests are booked into your reservation calendar. For rooms, we connect to your property management system or booking engine through the vendor's API where one is available, or the agent sends the guest a link to book on your own website. We confirm which route fits on the first call. Q: Is it safe to take deposits through an AI agent? A: The agents never take card details. They send a secure payment link from your own payment provider, so guests never need to read out or type a card number. Payment card security stays with your provider and your PCI DSS setup."},{"id":"k219","title":"AI agents for hotels and restaurants: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/hospitality/","text":"Q: How does it handle allergy and dietary questions? A: It answers only from the allergen and dietary information you approve for each dish, and it always says it cannot guarantee a dish is free of an allergen. Guests with severe allergies are asked to speak to staff, and the question is flagged to the team on shift. Q: Can it reply in our guests' languages? A: The WhatsApp agent replies in the language the guest writes in, including Arabic and Urdu. For phone calls we set up and test the languages you need before launch."},{"id":"k220","title":"AI agents for hotels and restaurants: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/hospitality/","text":"Q: Which review sites does it cover? A: The reputation agent works with Google Business Profile, Facebook and Trustpilot through their official APIs. For other platforms we check whether official access is available and confirm what can be connected on the first call. Q: Will guests know they are talking to an AI? A: Yes. The greeting says it is the hotel's or restaurant's AI assistant, and a guest can ask for a person at any time to be transferred or called back."},{"id":"k221","title":"AI agents for hotels and restaurants: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/hospitality/","text":"Q: How long does it take to go live? A: About two weeks. Many venues start with WhatsApp questions and bookings, review the first week of chats with us, and then add calls, reviews and social posts."},{"id":"k222","title":"Industries: AI agents for farms and agribusinesses","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/agriculture/","text":"Visionbotix builds AI solutions for agriculture: computer vision and IoT sensors that monitor animals, fields and equipment, and AI agents that answer questions from your farm data, reply to buyers on WhatsApp and handle orders and traceability paperwork. Agents go live in two to four weeks; vision and IoT builds have their own project timeline. Rules we design around: Farm data ownership and access (Global), GDPR and UK GDPR (EU · UK), Food traceability records (EU · UK · US), Farm assurance and buyer audits (Global). Data Analyst Agent from $3,000 + $399/mo."},{"id":"k223","title":"AI agents for farms and agribusinesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/agriculture/","text":"Q: Do you only set up agents, or can you build computer vision and IoT for our farm? A: Both. We build custom computer vision and IoT systems, from cameras over pens and parlors to soil, climate and water sensors, and connect them to a dashboard and alerts. A smart dairy farm project of ours records each animal's weight, temperature, milk yield, fat content and feed automatically. The agents then work on top of that data. Q: What is Smart Livestock? A: Smart Livestock is our own livestock monitoring system for dairy and livestock farms. Computer vision and IoT sensors record each animal's daily readings, and a dashboard flags health and yield problems early. You can see it at livestock.visionbotix.com or read how the smart dairy farm system was built."},{"id":"k224","title":"AI agents for farms and agribusinesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/agriculture/","text":"Q: Our farm has a weak internet connection. Will this work? A: Yes, when it is designed for it. Vision models and sensor gateways run on site on edge devices such as NVIDIA Jetson or Raspberry Pi, keep recording when the connection drops and sync when it returns. Sensors use LoRa, cellular or Wi-Fi links chosen for your range and power. Q: Can the AI tell us which animal is sick? A: It flags animals whose readings, such as temperature, feed intake or milk yield, move outside their normal range, and sends the alert with the history behind it. It does not diagnose. The farm manager or vet decides what is wrong and what to do."},{"id":"k225","title":"AI agents for farms and agribusinesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/agriculture/","text":"Q: Do we have to replace our herd or farm management software? A: No. The agents work alongside the systems you already use, through their API, a database connection or regular exports. If a system has no safe way in, we tell you on the first call instead of building something fragile. Q: Who owns the data from our sensors and cameras? A: You do. It is stored in your own cloud account or on your premises, you can export it at any time, and AI providers are set not to train on it. Ownership and access are written into the contract before any device goes in."},{"id":"k226","title":"AI agents for farms and agribusinesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/agriculture/","text":"Q: Can workers and buyers use it in their own language? A: Yes. The WhatsApp agent replies in the language the customer writes in, including Arabic and Urdu, and understands voice notes. The knowledge agent answers workers in English, Arabic and other major languages from your own procedures."},{"id":"k227","title":"Industries: AI agents for startups and SaaS teams","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/saas-startups/","text":"Visionbotix helps startups and SaaS teams build and grow AI products. Our fixed-price AI MVP Sprint takes an idea to launch with you owning the code. After launch, AI agents resolve support tickets, research accounts and book sales meetings, and grow your search and AI visibility. Agents go live in about two weeks; the MVP Sprint runs 6–8 weeks. Rules we design around: SOC 2 readiness (US), GDPR, UK GDPR and CCPA (EU · UK · US), EU AI Act (EU), LLM security reviews (Global), CAN-SPAM, CASL and PECR (US · Canada · UK). AI MVP Sprint from $12,000."},{"id":"k228","title":"AI agents for startups and SaaS teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/saas-startups/","text":"Q: What can you realistically build in a 6–8 week AI MVP Sprint? A: One core user journey done properly, with sign-in, an admin area and the AI features that make the product valuable. A one-week discovery cuts everything else to a later list and fixes the scope and price in writing. See the AI MVP Sprint for the full plan. Q: Can you add AI to the SaaS product we already have? A: Yes. We build copilots, smart search, document processing and agents inside your product, with per-tenant data isolation, evals and cost limits. That can run as a fixed-scope sprint or with a dedicated team working in your own repository."},{"id":"k229","title":"AI agents for startups and SaaS teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/saas-startups/","text":"Q: Have you shipped an AI product of your own? A: Yes. We built and run Wakeel, an AI legal matching platform where people describe a problem in Urdu, English or Roman Urdu and the AI matches them with verified advocates. It uses the same prompt-first interface, extraction and matching we build for startups. Q: Do we own the code, and will you sign an NDA? A: Yes to both. We sign an NDA from the first call, and the code, IP, repository and cloud accounts are yours at handover. We can set everything up in your name from day one if you prefer."},{"id":"k230","title":"AI agents for startups and SaaS teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/saas-startups/","text":"Q: Which AI models do you use, and can we switch later? A: Whichever fits on quality, speed, cost and data rules, usually OpenAI or Anthropic models, or an open model when data must stay in your cloud. The model sits behind a thin layer with evals around it, so you can switch later without a rewrite. Q: Will an AI support agent frustrate our users? A: It answers only from your docs and account data, says when it does not know and hands the ticket to your team with a summary. Users can ask for a person at any time, and we test it on your real past tickets before launch."},{"id":"k231","title":"AI agents for startups and SaaS teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/saas-startups/","text":"Q: Will AI outbound hurt our email domain? A: It is set up to protect it, with daily sending limits, inbox warm-up, suppression lists and an optional separate sending domain. Every email is researched for that account and approved by a person, so it reads like a real message rather than a blast."},{"id":"k232","title":"Industries: AI agents for government and defense teams","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/government-defense/","text":"Visionbotix builds secure AI for government and defense teams. Knowledge and document agents run on-premise or air-gapped with open-weight models, so data stays in your network, and every AI system is red-teamed before use. Our VX-1 encryptor, ThreatIQ and Cyber Range protect the network around it. Agents go live in two to four weeks; hardware is scoped per deployment. Rules we design around: Data sovereignty and residency (Global), Air-gapped operation (Global), NIST AI RMF (US), EU AI Act (EU), Public procurement and audit (Global). Knowledge Agent from $3,500 + $399/mo."},{"id":"k233","title":"AI agents for government and defense teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/government-defense/","text":"Q: Can the AI run fully air-gapped, with no internet connection? A: Yes. We deploy on your own servers with an open-weight model, so no document, question or answer leaves your network. Hosted models are stronger on some tasks, so we help you choose per use case and test the chosen model on your own questions before go-live. Q: How do you stop the AI from leaking data or being manipulated? A: Permissions are checked against your identity provider on every question, and tool results are treated as untrusted input. Before go-live we red-team the system for prompt injection, jailbreaks, data leakage and tool misuse, and you get a written report with fixes and a retest."},{"id":"k234","title":"AI agents for government and defense teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/government-defense/","text":"Q: What are the VX-1, ThreatIQ and Cyber Range? A: They are our own security products. The VX-1 IP Encryptor encrypts traffic between sites with AES-256 in FPGA hardware, ThreatIQ defends air-gapped networks from the inside, and the Cyber Range trains red and blue teams and benchmarks network devices. Q: Can the AI make decisions about citizens or cases? A: We design it to prepare, check and summarize, not to decide. Uncertain fields go to a reviewer, and any decision that affects a person stays with your staff, with the agent's work logged so it can be reviewed later."},{"id":"k235","title":"AI agents for government and defense teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/industries/government-defense/","text":"Q: Will it work with our existing systems? A: Usually, yes. The agents connect to SharePoint, network file shares, Confluence, ticketing and case systems with an API, and your identity provider for sign-in. If a system has no safe way in, the document agent can produce validated import files instead. Q: How do you handle confidentiality? A: We sign an NDA from the first call, project material is seen only by the engineers working on it, and we never name customers or describe their deployments in public. Data stays in your environment wherever the deployment allows it."},{"id":"k236","title":"Where we work (country pages): AI agents and software for US companies","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/","text":"Visionbotix builds AI agents, web apps and SaaS products for US companies. Our project shift covers most of the East Coast working day and the West Coast morning, every price is public in US dollars, and US rules are designed in: BAA-signing providers for health data, TCPA consent checks on every call and text, and hosting in a US region. Live overlap: New York 7 h (09:00–16:00 ET), Chicago 6 h (09:00–15:00 CT), Los Angeles 4 h (09:00–13:00 PT). Rules we design around: HIPAA, TCPA and the FCC AI voice ruling, CCPA/CPRA and state privacy laws, FTC rule on fake reviews, Colorado AI law (SB 26-189)."},{"id":"k237","title":"AI agents and software for US companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/","text":"Q: How much does an AI agent cost in the USA? A: Our packaged agents start from $750 setup plus $199 a month (the Reputation Agent). Popular with US companies: the Receptionist Agent from about $1,500 plus $349 a month and the Booking Agent from about $1,500 plus $299 a month. Custom agents start from $8,000, fixed price after scoping, and the AI Opportunity Audit is $490, credited in full against a build. Your fixed quote states the exact amount before any work starts. Q: Do you have an office in the US? A: No. Our team works from our studio in Rawalpindi, Pakistan, and we do not use a virtual US address. Calls run on Zoom, Teams or Google Meet inside US working hours, and every project has one named lead you can reach the same day."},{"id":"k238","title":"AI agents and software for US companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/","text":"Q: Which hours will your team work on my project? A: Projects for US clients run from 17:00 to 02:00 Pakistan time, which is 07:00 to 16:00 in New York in winter and 08:00 to 17:00 during daylight saving time. That gives East Coast teams seven hours of live overlap in winter, Chicago six and Los Angeles the morning, from 09:00 to 13:00 Pacific. Q: Will you sign a BAA for our practice? A: Yes, for any project where our team or our agents handle protected health information. We also run the agents on cloud and model providers that sign a BAA with us, keep PHI out of model training and document the data flow. HIPAA compliance stays your practice's responsibility, so your privacy officer signs off the setup."},{"id":"k239","title":"AI agents and software for US companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/","text":"Q: Is it legal for an AI agent to call or text our leads? A: Yes, with the right consent. The FCC treats AI-generated voices as artificial voices under the TCPA, so outbound AI calls need prior express consent, and marketing calls and texts need it in writing. We set the agents to contact only leads with consent on record, keep to calling hours and honor opt-outs at once. Your lawyer should confirm the consent wording on your forms. Q: Do you have a SOC 2 report? A: No, we do not hold a SOC 2 report. We answer your security questionnaire, document access control, encryption and logging, and can deploy the agents into your own AWS, Azure or Google Cloud account so your existing controls and audits cover them."},{"id":"k240","title":"AI agents and software for US companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/","text":"Q: Can the receptionist answer in Spanish? A: Yes. The agent can greet in English and switch to Spanish when the caller does, using the same approved answers in both languages. We test it with sample calls in both before it goes live, and callers can ask for a person at any time. Q: Do you need a W-9 from us, or do we need one from you? A: Neither. We are a company based in Pakistan, so we give you a completed Form W-8BEN-E instead of a W-9, and our engineers do the work from Pakistan. Your accountant confirms any withholding or state tax treatment for your business."},{"id":"k241","title":"Where we work (country pages): AI agents and software for UK businesses","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/","text":"Visionbotix builds AI agents, web and mobile apps and SaaS products for UK businesses. Projects run on a shift that overlaps the UK working day, every price is public and shown in pounds, and UK GDPR is designed in from the first sprint: UK hosting, processor terms and an IDTA for any data our engineers handle. Live overlap: London 7 h (09:00–16:00 GMT). Rules we design around: UK GDPR and DPA 2018, Data (Use and Access) Act 2025, PECR, DMCC Act 2024."},{"id":"k242","title":"AI agents and software for UK businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/","text":"Q: How much does an AI agent cost in the UK? A: Our packaged agents start from about £565 setup plus £150 a month (the Reputation Agent). Popular with UK businesses: the Receptionist Agent from about £1,150 plus £260 a month and the Booking Agent from about £1,150 plus £225 a month. Custom agents start from about £6,000, fixed price after scoping, and the AI Opportunity Audit is about £370, credited in full against a build. Our prices are set in US dollars; these figures are approximate at £0.75 per US$1, November 2026. Your fixed quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Do you have an office in the UK? A: No. Our team works from our studio in Rawalpindi, Pakistan, and we do not use a virtual UK address. Calls run on Teams, Zoom or Google Meet inside UK working hours, and every project has one named lead you can reach the same day."},{"id":"k243","title":"AI agents and software for UK businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/","text":"Q: Is it legal to send UK personal data to a team in Pakistan? A: Yes, with the right safeguards. Pakistan has no UK adequacy regulations, so where our engineers can access personal data we sign the ICO's International Data Transfer Agreement or the UK Addendum to the EU standard contractual clauses and complete a transfer risk assessment. In practice most work uses test data, and live data stays in your UK cloud region. Q: Which hours will your team work on my project? A: Projects for UK clients run from 12:00 to 21:00 Pakistan time, which is 07:00 to 16:00 in London in winter and 08:00 to 17:00 during British Summer Time. That gives you seven hours of live overlap in winter and the whole working day in summer."},{"id":"k244","title":"AI agents and software for UK businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/","text":"Q: Do you charge UK VAT? A: No UK VAT is added to our invoices. For VAT-registered UK businesses buying our services, the reverse charge usually applies, so you account for the VAT on your own return. Your accountant confirms the treatment for your business. Q: Can the receptionist speak with a British voice? A: Yes. We choose a natural British English voice with you, load your business details and test the agent with sample calls in the accents your callers use before it goes live. Callers are told they are speaking to an AI assistant and can ask for a person at any time."},{"id":"k245","title":"AI agents and software for UK businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/","text":"Q: Who owns the code and the data? A: You do. The contract gives you full ownership of the code, the prompts, the configuration and the data from the first milestone payment. We hand over the repositories and a recorded walkthrough at the end of the project."},{"id":"k246","title":"Where we work (country pages): AI agents and software for Canadian companies","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/canada/","text":"Visionbotix builds AI agents and web apps for Canadian companies. Agents work in English and French, data stays in a Canadian cloud region, and PIPEDA, Quebec's Law 25 and CASL are designed in from the first sprint. Our project shift covers most of the Toronto working day and the Vancouver morning, and every price is public. Live overlap: Toronto 7 h (09:00–16:00 ET), Calgary 5 h (09:00–14:00 MT), Vancouver 4 h (09:00–13:00 PT). Rules we design around: PIPEDA, Quebec Law 25, CASL, Charter of the French Language, PHIPA and provincial health laws."},{"id":"k247","title":"AI agents and software for Canadian companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/canada/","text":"Q: How much does an AI agent cost in Canada? A: Our packaged agents start from about CA$1,050 setup plus CA$280 a month (the Reputation Agent). Popular with Canadian companies: the Receptionist Agent from about CA$2,100 plus CA$490 a month and the Support Agent from about CA$3,500 plus CA$630 a month. Custom agents start from about CA$11,000, fixed price after scoping, and the AI Opportunity Audit is about CA$685, credited in full against a build. Our prices are set in US dollars; these figures are approximate at CA$1.40 per US$1, November 2026. Your fixed quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Do you have an office in Canada? A: No. Our team works from our studio in Rawalpindi, Pakistan, and we do not use a virtual Canadian address. Calls run on Teams, Zoom or Google Meet inside Canadian working hours, and every project has one named lead you can reach the same day."},{"id":"k248","title":"AI agents and software for Canadian companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/canada/","text":"Q: Which hours will your team work on my project? A: Projects for Canadian clients run from 17:00 to 02:00 Pakistan time, which is 07:00 to 16:00 in Toronto in winter and 08:00 to 17:00 during daylight saving time. That gives Toronto seven hours of live overlap in winter, Calgary five and Vancouver the morning, from 09:00 to 13:00 Pacific. Q: Can the agents serve our Quebec customers in French? A: Yes. The agent answers in French or English, switches when the customer does and uses the same approved answers in both languages. A French speaker on your side reviews the French scripts and knowledge base before launch, and callers can ask for a person at any time."},{"id":"k249","title":"AI agents and software for Canadian companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/canada/","text":"Q: Can our data stay in Canada? A: Yes. We deploy the agents and their data in a Canadian region of AWS, Azure or Google Cloud, in your account or ours, and choose model providers that process data in Canada where your policy requires it. We document every place the data goes so your privacy officer can sign it off. Q: Does Quebec's Law 25 allow a team in Pakistan to work on our data? A: Yes, with an assessment first. Law 25 asks you to complete a privacy impact assessment before personal information is communicated outside Quebec, including to a service provider. We give you the data-flow details and safeguards it needs. In practice most of our work uses test data, and live records stay in your Canadian region."},{"id":"k250","title":"AI agents and software for Canadian companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/canada/","text":"Q: Is there a Canadian AI law we must follow? A: Canada has no federal AI-specific law in force; the proposed Artificial Intelligence and Data Act died with Bill C-27 when Parliament was prorogued in January 2025. Privacy laws already apply to how agents use personal data, and Quebec's Law 25 adds the notice for fully automated decisions, which we build in. Q: Do you charge GST or HST? A: No GST, HST or QST is added to our invoices, which come from Pakistan. Some Canadian businesses must self-assess tax on services imported from abroad, depending on how they use them. Your accountant confirms the treatment for your business."},{"id":"k251","title":"Where we work (country pages): AI agents and software for Australian businesses","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/","text":"Visionbotix builds AI agents, mobile apps and SaaS products for Australian businesses, from receptionists that answer every call to booking and review agents. Our shift covers your afternoon on the east coast and most of the day in Perth, prices are shown in Australian dollars, and Privacy Act safeguards come first: Australian hosting and APP 8 contract terms. Live overlap: Sydney 4 h (13:00–17:00 AEDT), Brisbane 5 h (12:00–17:00 AEST), Perth 7 h (10:00–17:00 AWST). Rules we design around: Privacy Act 1988 and the APPs, Automated decisions in privacy policies, Spam Act and Do Not Call Register, Australian Consumer Law, Statutory privacy tort."},{"id":"k252","title":"AI agents and software for Australian businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/","text":"Q: How much does an AI agent cost in Australia? A: Our packaged agents start from about A$1,150 setup plus A$300 a month (the Reputation Agent). Popular with Australian businesses: the Receptionist Agent from about A$2,250 plus A$525 a month and the Booking Agent from about A$2,250 plus A$450 a month. Custom agents start from about A$12,000, fixed price after scoping, and the AI Opportunity Audit is about A$735, credited in full against a build. Our prices are set in US dollars; these figures are approximate at A$1.50 per US$1, November 2026. Your fixed quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Do you have an office in Australia? A: No. Our team works from our studio in Rawalpindi, Pakistan, and we do not use a virtual Australian address. Calls run on Teams, Zoom or Google Meet inside your working hours, and every project has one named lead you can reach the same day."},{"id":"k253","title":"AI agents and software for Australian businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/","text":"Q: Can our customers' personal information be accessed from Pakistan? A: Only with safeguards in place. Under APP 8 your business must take reasonable steps before personal information leaves Australia, and it stays accountable for how the overseas recipient handles it. So we sign contract terms that bind us to the Australian Privacy Principles, keep live data in your Australian cloud region and work with test data wherever we can. Q: Which hours will your team work on my project? A: Projects for Australian clients run from 07:00 to 16:00 Pakistan time. In Sydney and Melbourne that is 13:00 to 22:00 during daylight saving and 12:00 to 21:00 from April to October, so you get four hours of live overlap in summer and five in winter. Brisbane gets five hours and Perth seven, all year."},{"id":"k254","title":"AI agents and software for Australian businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/","text":"Q: Do you charge GST? A: No Australian GST is added to our invoices. When a GST-registered Australian business buys services from an overseas supplier, the buyer works out whether GST applies, and in most cases it only does if you could not claim a full credit for the purchase. Your accountant confirms the treatment for your business. Q: Is there an AI law in Australia we need to follow? A: Australia has no AI-specific Act yet, so AI agents fall under existing laws such as the Privacy Act, the Australian Consumer Law and the Spam Act. The Government's voluntary Guidance for AI Adoption sets out six essential practices for using AI responsibly, and we use it as a checklist when we plan an agent with you."},{"id":"k255","title":"AI agents and software for Australian businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/","text":"Q: Can the receptionist sound Australian? A: Yes. We choose a natural Australian English voice with you, load your business details and test the agent with sample calls in the accents your callers use before it goes live. Callers are told they are speaking to an AI assistant and can ask for a person at any time."},{"id":"k256","title":"Where we work (country pages): AI agents and software for German companies","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/germany/","text":"Visionbotix builds AI agents and custom software for German companies, from knowledge and document agents to dedicated engineering teams. Our shift covers your whole working day, agents answer in German and English, and GDPR and the EU AI Act are designed in: an Art. 28 processing agreement, EU standard contractual clauses and hosting in Frankfurt. Live overlap: Berlin 8 h (09:00–17:00 CET). Rules we design around: GDPR and BDSG, EU AI Act, Works council (BetrVG §87), TDDDG cookie consent, NIS2 and the BSI Act."},{"id":"k257","title":"AI agents and software for German companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/germany/","text":"Q: How much does an AI agent cost in Germany? A: Our packaged agents start from about €685 setup plus €180 a month (the Reputation Agent). Popular with German companies: the Knowledge Agent from about €3,200 plus €365 a month and the Document Agent from about €2,750 plus €365 a month. Custom agents start from about €7,300, fixed price after scoping, and the AI Opportunity Audit is about €445, credited in full against a build. Our prices are set in US dollars; these figures are approximate at €0.91 per US$1, November 2026. Your fixed quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Do you have an office in Germany? A: No. Our team works from our studio in Rawalpindi, Pakistan, and we do not use a virtual German address. Calls run on Teams, Zoom or Google Meet inside German working hours, and every project has one named lead you can reach the same day."},{"id":"k258","title":"AI agents and software for German companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/germany/","text":"Q: Is it allowed under GDPR for engineers in Pakistan to access our data? A: Yes, with the right safeguards. There is no EU adequacy decision for Pakistan, so where our engineers can access personal data we sign the 2021 EU standard contractual clauses alongside the Art. 28 agreement and complete a transfer impact assessment with you. In practice most work uses test data, and live data stays in your EU cloud region. Q: Which hours will your team work on my project? A: Projects for German clients run from 12:00 to 21:00 Pakistan time, which is 08:00 to 17:00 in Germany in winter and 09:00 to 18:00 during summer time. That gives you eight hours of live overlap all year, the whole working day."},{"id":"k259","title":"AI agents and software for German companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/germany/","text":"Q: Do you charge German VAT? A: No German VAT is added to our invoices. For businesses in Germany buying our services, the reverse charge under §13b UStG usually applies, so you account for the VAT on your own return. Your Steuerberater confirms the treatment for your business. Q: Does our works council have to agree before we roll out an AI agent? A: Often, yes. Under §87(1) no. 6 BetrVG the works council has a say on technical systems that can monitor employees, and an assistant that logs who asked what usually counts. We give you a plain description of the data each agent processes and logs, and adjust the setup to what you agree in the works agreement."},{"id":"k260","title":"AI agents and software for German companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/germany/","text":"Q: Does the EU AI Act apply to a support or knowledge agent? A: Yes, mostly through transparency. Since August 2026 people must be told when they are dealing with an AI, so our agents say so. Uses such as recruitment or credit decisions count as high-risk, with most of those duties starting in December 2027. We map each use case to its risk class before we build. Q: Can the agents answer in German? A: Yes. Agents answer in German and English and follow the language the person writes or speaks in. We agree with you whether they use the formal Sie or the informal du, load your terminology and test with sample conversations before go-live."},{"id":"k261","title":"Where we work (country pages): AI agents and software for UAE businesses","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/","text":"Visionbotix builds AI agents, WhatsApp automation and mobile apps for UAE businesses. Our team works 09:00 to 18:00 Dubai time, one hour behind Rawalpindi. Agents reply in Arabic and English with right-to-left chat, prices are shown in dirhams, and data can stay in a UAE cloud region under the federal PDPL, DIFC or ADGM rules. Live overlap: Dubai 8 h (09:00–17:00 GST). Rules we design around: UAE PDPL, DIFC Data Protection Law 2020, ADGM Data Protection Regulations 2021, UAE health data law, Telemarketing rules 2024."},{"id":"k262","title":"AI agents and software for UAE businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/","text":"Q: How much does an AI agent cost in the UAE? A: Our packaged agents start from about AED 2,750 setup plus AED 730 a month (the Reputation Agent). Popular with UAE businesses: the WhatsApp Agent from about AED 5,500 plus AED 1,100 a month and the Receptionist Agent from about AED 5,500 plus AED 1,300 a month. Custom agents start from about AED 29,500, fixed price after scoping, and the AI Opportunity Audit is about AED 1,800, credited in full against a build. Our prices are set in US dollars; these figures are approximate at AED 3.6725 per US$1, November 2026. Your fixed quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Do you have an office in the UAE? A: No. Our team works from our studio in Rawalpindi, Pakistan, and we do not use a virtual UAE address or a free zone license. Calls run on Teams, Zoom or Google Meet inside UAE working hours, and every project has one named lead you can reach the same day."},{"id":"k263","title":"AI agents and software for UAE businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/","text":"Q: Can the agents speak Arabic? A: Yes. WhatsApp, chat and voice agents reply in Arabic or English, following the language the customer uses, and web and app chat shows Arabic right to left. Answers still come only from your approved content, and we review the Arabic replies with your team before launch. Q: We are in the DIFC or ADGM. Does that change anything? A: It changes which data protection law applies. Onshore businesses follow the federal PDPL, DIFC firms the DIFC Data Protection Law 2020 and its Regulation 10 on AI systems, and ADGM firms the ADGM Data Protection Regulations 2021. We set up the processor terms and transfer safeguards for the regime you are under, and your DPO signs off the setup before go-live."},{"id":"k264","title":"AI agents and software for UAE businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/","text":"Q: Can our data stay in the UAE? A: Yes. Agents and data can run in a UAE cloud region such as AWS Middle East (UAE) or Azure UAE North, and health data stays in the country as the health data law generally requires. Our engineers work on test data, and where they need to see personal data we sign the transfer terms first. Q: Which hours will your team work on my project? A: Projects for UAE clients run from 10:00 to 19:00 Pakistan time, which is 09:00 to 18:00 in Dubai and Abu Dhabi. That gives you eight hours of live overlap with a 09:00 to 17:00 day, all year, because neither country uses daylight saving. We work Monday to Friday, like most UAE businesses."},{"id":"k265","title":"AI agents and software for UAE businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/","text":"Q: Do you charge UAE VAT? A: No UAE VAT is added to our invoices. For VAT-registered UAE businesses, services imported from abroad usually fall under the reverse charge, so you account for the VAT on your own return. Your tax adviser confirms the treatment for your business. Q: Who owns the code and the data? A: You do. The contract gives you full ownership of the code, the prompts, the configuration and the data from the first milestone payment. We hand over the repositories and a recorded walkthrough at the end of the project."},{"id":"k266","title":"Where we work (country pages): AI agents and software for Saudi companies","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/","text":"Visionbotix builds AI agents, generative AI and mobile apps for Saudi companies. Our team works 08:00 to 17:00 Riyadh time, sharing Monday to Thursday with your week. Agents reply in Arabic and English with right-to-left chat, prices are shown in riyals, and setups follow the PDPL and SDAIA's transfer rules, with data in an in-Kingdom cloud region. Live overlap: Riyadh 8 h (09:00–17:00 AST). Rules we design around: Personal Data Protection Law, Data transfer regulation, NCA Essential Cybersecurity Controls, SAMA Cyber Security Framework, SDAIA AI Ethics Principles."},{"id":"k267","title":"AI agents and software for Saudi companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/","text":"Q: How much does an AI agent cost in Saudi Arabia? A: Our packaged agents start from about SAR 2,800 setup plus SAR 745 a month (the Reputation Agent). Popular with Saudi companies: the WhatsApp Agent from about SAR 5,650 plus SAR 1,100 a month and the Support Agent from about SAR 9,400 plus SAR 1,700 a month. Custom agents start from about SAR 30,000, fixed price after scoping, and the AI Opportunity Audit is about SAR 1,850, credited in full against a build. Our prices are set in US dollars; these figures are approximate at SAR 3.75 per US$1, November 2026. Your fixed quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Do you have an office in Saudi Arabia? A: No. Our team works from our studio in Rawalpindi, Pakistan, and we do not use a virtual Saudi address. Calls run on Teams, Zoom or Google Meet inside Saudi working hours, and every project has one named lead you can reach the same day."},{"id":"k268","title":"AI agents and software for Saudi companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/","text":"Q: Do you work on Sundays? A: Our team works Monday to Friday, so Monday to Thursday overlap your working week. If your project needs Sunday cover, for a launch or a support rota, we agree it in the contract before work starts. Your AI agents run every day, Fridays and Saturdays included. Q: Which hours will your team work on my project? A: Projects for Saudi clients run from 10:00 to 19:00 Pakistan time, which is 08:00 to 17:00 in Riyadh, Jeddah and Dammam. That gives you eight hours of live overlap with a 09:00 to 17:00 day, all year, because neither country uses daylight saving."},{"id":"k269","title":"AI agents and software for Saudi companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/","text":"Q: Can our data stay in Saudi Arabia? A: Yes. Agents and data can run in an in-Kingdom cloud region or on your own servers, and our engineers work on test data. Where they need to see personal data, we sign SDAIA's standard contractual clauses and support your transfer risk assessment under the PDPL. Q: Can the agents work in Arabic? A: Yes. Agents reply in Arabic or English, following the language the customer uses, and web and app chat shows Arabic right to left. The knowledge assistant and document agent also read Arabic documents. We review the Arabic replies with your team before launch."},{"id":"k270","title":"AI agents and software for Saudi companies: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/","text":"Q: Can you build for government entities? A: Yes, when the work fits the entity's security rules, including the NCA's Essential Cybersecurity Controls. Agents run on-premise or air-gapped with open-weight models, so data never leaves your network, and our team works only with the access your security team approves. Q: Who owns the code and the data? A: You do. The contract gives you full ownership of the code, the prompts, the configuration and the data from the first milestone payment. We hand over the repositories and a recorded walkthrough at the end of the project."},{"id":"k271","title":"Where we work (country pages): AI agents and software for Pakistani businesses","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/","text":"Visionbotix is a software house in Rawalpindi, a short drive from Islamabad, building AI agents, mobile apps and custom software for Pakistani businesses. WhatsApp and chat agents reply in Urdu, Roman Urdu and English, prices are shown in rupees, and teams in the twin cities can meet us in person at our studio on Murree Road. Live overlap: Islamabad 7 h (10:00–17:00 PKT). Rules we design around: PECA 2016 and 2025 amendments, Personal Data Protection Bill, State Bank outsourcing rules, National AI Policy 2025."},{"id":"k272","title":"AI agents and software for Pakistani businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/","text":"Q: How much does an AI agent cost in Pakistan? A: Our packaged agents start from about PKR 210,000 setup plus PKR 55,500 a month (the Reputation Agent). Popular with Pakistani businesses: the WhatsApp Agent from about PKR 420,000 plus PKR 83,500 a month and the Support Agent from about PKR 700,000 plus PKR 125,000 a month. Custom agents start from about PKR 2,250,000, fixed price after scoping, and the AI Opportunity Audit is about PKR 135,000, credited in full against a build. Our prices are set in US dollars; these figures are approximate at PKR 280 per US$1, November 2026. Your fixed quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Can we meet your team in person? A: Yes. Our studio is on the second floor of Meridian Software Technology Park, Satellite Town, Murree Road, Rawalpindi. Teams in Islamabad and Rawalpindi can hold the kick-off and milestone reviews with us face to face. Teams in other cities meet us on Teams, Zoom or Google Meet, with the same named lead and weekly demo."},{"id":"k273","title":"AI agents and software for Pakistani businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/","text":"Q: Can the agent reply in Roman Urdu? A: Yes. The WhatsApp and chat agents reply in the language the customer writes in, including Urdu, Roman Urdu, English and messages that mix them, and they understand voice notes. Answers still come only from your approved catalogue and policies, and we test the Urdu and Roman Urdu replies with your team before launch. Q: Is there a data protection law in Pakistan? A: Not yet. The Personal Data Protection Bill is still a draft, so PECA 2016 and sector rules such as the State Bank's apply today. We set up every agent as if the bill were law already, with clear purposes, access controls, audit logs and customer data kept out of model training, so you are ready if it becomes law."},{"id":"k274","title":"AI agents and software for Pakistani businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/","text":"Q: Will our data leave Pakistan? A: Only if you choose a setup where it does. Many AI model providers process data abroad, so for sensitive records we can run an open-weight model on your own servers or in a data centre in Pakistan. Your regulator's rules and your policy decide the hosting, and we write it into the contract. Q: Which hours does your team work? A: Our team works from 10:00 to 19:00 Pakistan time, Monday to Friday, which gives you seven hours of live overlap with a 09:00 to 17:00 office day. Your AI agents run every day, including weekends and public holidays."},{"id":"k275","title":"AI agents and software for Pakistani businesses: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/","text":"Q: Have you built products for Pakistan before? A: Yes, our own. Wakeel is an AI lawyer-matching platform where people describe a legal problem in Urdu, English or Roman Urdu, by typing or speaking, and are shown verified advocates. Smart Livestock monitors dairy and livestock farms with computer vision and sensors. We describe client work only on a call, under NDA. Q: Who owns the code and the data? A: You do. The contract gives you full ownership of the code, the prompts, the configuration and the data from the first milestone payment. We hand over the repositories and a recorded walkthrough at the end of the project."},{"id":"k276","title":"AI agents set up for one country (local rules, systems and prices): Receptionist Agent in ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/ai-receptionist/","text":"Our AI receptionist for Australian businesses answers every call in an Australian English voice, books into Cliniko, Halaxy, ServiceM8 or your calendar, and puts urgent calls through to a person. It is set up for your state's public holidays, triple zero guidance, call recording and Spam Act rules, and stores call data in Australia. Prices below in Australian dollars. Local rules: Privacy Act 1988 and the APPs, Recording phone calls, Spam Act 2003 for texts, Telemarketing industry standard. Systems: Cliniko, Halaxy, ServiceM8, simPRO, Google Calendar, Microsoft 365 / Outlook, Calendly, Cal.com, HubSpot, Zoho CRM, Salesforce."},{"id":"k277","title":"Receptionist Agent in Australia: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: How much does the Receptionist Agent cost in Australia? A: Setup is about A$2,250, then about A$525 a month for hosting, monitoring, weekly tuning and a fair-use volume of usage. Usage above that (call minutes, WhatsApp conversation fees, AI model costs) is passed through at cost with no markup, and we tell you before it happens. Our prices are set in US dollars (US$1,500 + US$349/mo); local figures are approximate at A$1.50 per US$1, November 2026, and your quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Can I keep my existing number, including a 1300 or 1800 number? A: Yes. You keep your number and forward calls to the agent through your phone provider, either all calls, only after hours or only when your lines are busy. A 1300 or 1800 number forwards the same way as a landline or mobile. If you want a separate line, we set up a new local number."},{"id":"k278","title":"Receptionist Agent in Australia: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Does it work with Dental4Windows or Core Practice? A: Possibly, but we check first. Access for outside booking tools is arranged through the vendor, so in the first week we confirm with the vendor whether a connection can be switched on for your practice. If it cannot, the agent takes the booking request with all the details and your team confirms the slot. Q: What does the agent do if someone calls with an emergency? A: For a life-threatening emergency, it tells the caller to hang up and call triple zero (000) and alerts your team straight away. For urgent but non-life-threatening calls, such as dental pain or a burst pipe, it follows your rules and either transfers the call, texts the on-call person or books the next urgent slot. It never gives medical advice."},{"id":"k279","title":"Receptionist Agent in Australia: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Is it legal to record calls in every state? A: Recording rules come from state and territory law as well as Commonwealth law, and they differ. That is why recording is off by default. When you turn it on, the greeting tells every caller the call is recorded, and recordings stay in your Australian account under your retention rules. Your own legal adviser can confirm the position for your state. Q: Can it answer bulk-billing and health fund questions? A: Yes, from the answers you approve, such as whether you bulk bill, which funds you are a preferred provider for and whether a gap applies. It does not quote a patient's own fees or process claims; those questions go to your front desk."},{"id":"k280","title":"Receptionist Agent in Australia: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/australia/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Will tradies get the job details they need? A: Yes. The agent asks for the address, the problem, access details and a contact number, creates the job in ServiceM8 or simPRO, and texts urgent callouts to the on-call mobile. Quotes and pricing questions beyond your approved list go to you. Q: Where is the call data stored? A: In an Australian cloud region, encrypted in transit and at rest, and kept out of model training. Transcripts follow your retention rules and access is role-based, so only the staff you choose can read them. Your privacy officer gets a data-flow document before go-live, which also shows where calls are processed."},{"id":"k281","title":"AI agents set up for one country (local rules, systems and prices): WhatsApp Agent in Paki","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Our WhatsApp chatbot for Pakistani businesses is an AI agent on the official WhatsApp Business Platform. It replies in Urdu, Roman Urdu and English, understands voice notes, confirms cash-on-delivery orders before you book the courier and shares TCS, Leopards or PostEx tracking. It follows Meta's opt-in and template rules and PECA's unsubscribe duty. Prices below are in rupees. Local rules: WhatsApp opt-in before you message first, The 24-hour customer service window, Escalation to a person and no card numbers, Meta's terms on AI providers, PECA 2016 spamming offence. Systems: Shopify, WooCommerce, TCS, Leopards Courier, PostEx, Google Sheets, Zoho CRM, HubSpot, WhatsApp Business Platform, Instagram Messaging API."},{"id":"k282","title":"WhatsApp Agent in Pakistan: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: How much does the WhatsApp Agent cost in Pakistan? A: Setup is about PKR 420,000, then about PKR 83,500 a month for hosting, monitoring, weekly tuning and a fair-use volume of usage. Usage above that (call minutes, WhatsApp conversation fees, AI model costs) is passed through at cost with no markup, and we tell you before it happens. Our prices are set in US dollars (US$1,500 + US$299/mo); local figures are approximate at PKR 280 per US$1, November 2026, and your quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Is this a WhatsApp chatbot or an AI agent? A: Both terms describe it, but it is more than a button menu. It reads free text and voice notes in Urdu, Roman Urdu and English, looks up stock and orders in your store and courier systems, and replies like a member of your team. Answers come only from your approved catalogue and policies."},{"id":"k283","title":"WhatsApp Agent in Pakistan: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Can it confirm cash-on-delivery orders? A: Yes. After each COD order, the agent sends a WhatsApp confirmation with the items, address and total, and the customer confirms or cancels in one reply. Each reply is logged against the Shopify or WooCommerce order, or in your order sheet, so your team books the courier only for confirmed orders and calls the unanswered ones. Q: Will it understand Roman Urdu and Urdu voice notes? A: Yes. It understands Roman Urdu in its many spellings, Urdu script, English and messages that mix them, as well as voice notes in Urdu, and it replies in text in the customer's language. We test the replies with your team before launch."},{"id":"k284","title":"WhatsApp Agent in Pakistan: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Could my number get banned? A: The common risk comes from unofficial bulk-sender software and modified WhatsApp apps, which break WhatsApp's terms. We build only on the official WhatsApp Business Platform, message people who opted in, use templates outside the 24-hour window and watch your number's quality rating. Q: Can I send offers to my whole contact list? A: Only to customers who opted in to hear from your business. Offers go out as marketing templates with an easy opt-out, as Meta's rules and PECA's unsubscribe duty require, and anyone who opts out is not messaged again. Buying number lists or messaging people who never opted in puts your number at risk."},{"id":"k285","title":"WhatsApp Agent in Pakistan: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/pakistan/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Which couriers can it track? A: TCS, Leopards Courier and PostEx through the API access your merchant account can request, and other couriers whose API or tracking service your account can use. The agent replies with the parcel status and tracking link, and delivery complaints go to your team. Q: What happens during Eid holidays when my team is away? A: The agent keeps answering product, order and tracking questions every day, tells customers your dispatch dates around Eid, and queues chats that need a person with a clear note of when your team will reply."},{"id":"k286","title":"AI agents set up for one country (local rules, systems and prices): WhatsApp Agent in Saud","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Our WhatsApp Agent answers Saudi shoppers and clients on WhatsApp in Arabic or English, day and night, with live order status from Salla, Zid or Shopify and your courier. It confirms cash-on-delivery orders and the National Address, sends offers only to opted-in customers, in line with the PDPL, and can keep data in the Kingdom. Prices below in riyals. Local rules: WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy, 24-hour window and approved templates, PDPL Article 25, consent for advertising, PDPL Article 29, transfers outside the Kingdom, E-Commerce Law rules for electronic ads. Systems: Salla, Zid, Shopify, WooCommerce, Magento, SMSA Express, Aramex, Naqel Express, HubSpot, Zoho CRM, Google Sheets, Google Calendar."},{"id":"k287","title":"WhatsApp Agent in Saudi Arabia: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: How much does the WhatsApp Agent cost in Saudi Arabia? A: Setup is about SAR 5,650, then about SAR 1,100 a month for hosting, monitoring, weekly tuning and a fair-use volume of usage. Usage above that (call minutes, WhatsApp conversation fees, AI model costs) is passed through at cost with no markup, and we tell you before it happens. Our prices are set in US dollars (US$1,500 + US$299/mo); local figures are approximate at SAR 3.75 per US$1, November 2026, and your quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Can it reply in Saudi dialect? A: Yes. It replies in Arabic to messages and voice notes in Saudi dialect, and we set the replies to Saudi phrasing or Modern Standard Arabic as you prefer. We test it on real messages from your chats and review the Arabic replies with your team before launch. Answers come only from your catalog and policies."},{"id":"k288","title":"WhatsApp Agent in Saudi Arabia: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Does it work with Salla and Zid? A: Yes. Salla and Zid are among the store platforms the agent connects to, alongside Shopify and WooCommerce. It reads products, stock, orders and tracking, so its answers match your store admin, and order changes beyond the limits you set wait for staff approval. Q: Can customers pay with mada, Tabby or Tamara in the chat? A: Not inside WhatsApp itself. The agent sends a link to your store's checkout, where customers pay with mada, a card, Tabby, Tamara or cash on delivery, as your store allows. Payment details never pass through the agent; it only sees from the order in your store whether it has been paid."},{"id":"k289","title":"WhatsApp Agent in Saudi Arabia: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Where is the data stored? A: Chat history, logs and order lookups can run in an in-Kingdom cloud region or on your own servers. Messages pass through Meta's WhatsApp servers on the way, which your privacy notice should mention. Our engineers work on test data and sign SDAIA's standard contractual clauses before seeing live records. Q: Can we send offers to all our customers on WhatsApp? A: Only to customers who agreed to receive them. Article 25 of the PDPL requires prior consent for advertising and a clear way to stop it, so offers go out as Meta-approved marketing templates to opted-in customers, each with an easy opt-out, and anyone who opts out is not messaged again."},{"id":"k290","title":"WhatsApp Agent in Saudi Arabia: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/saudi-arabia/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Does it keep working on Fridays, Saturdays and in Ramadan? A: Yes. The agent runs every day, including the weekend, Ramadan nights and Eid. We switch it to your Ramadan hours and delivery cut-offs, add iftar and suhoor timings for restaurants, and chats that need a person wait in your inbox until your team is back. Q: Does it understand voice notes? A: Yes. Customers can send a voice note in Arabic or English, and the agent answers in text. If it is unsure what was said, it asks the customer to confirm or hands the chat to your team with the recording attached."},{"id":"k291","title":"AI agents set up for one country (local rules, systems and prices): WhatsApp Agent in the ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Our WhatsApp Agent answers UAE customers on WhatsApp in Arabic or English, shares live order status from your store and courier, confirms cash-on-delivery orders and the delivery location and books viewings or appointments. It follows Meta's opt-in and template rules, can keep chat data in a UAE region and goes live in about two weeks. Prices below in dirhams. Local rules: WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy, 24-hour window and approved templates, UAE Personal Data Protection Law, DIFC Regulation 10 on AI systems, Telemarketing calls, Cabinet Resolution 56 of 2024. Systems: Shopify, WooCommerce, Magento, Aramex, Quiqup, Shipa, DHL Express, HubSpot, Zoho CRM, Google Sheets, Google Calendar."},{"id":"k292","title":"WhatsApp Agent in the UAE: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: How much does the WhatsApp Agent cost in the UAE? A: Setup is about AED 5,500, then about AED 1,100 a month for hosting, monitoring, weekly tuning and a fair-use volume of usage. Usage above that (call minutes, WhatsApp conversation fees, AI model costs) is passed through at cost with no markup, and we tell you before it happens. Our prices are set in US dollars (US$1,500 + US$299/mo); local figures are approximate at AED 3.6725 per US$1, November 2026, and your quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Can it reply in Gulf Arabic? A: Yes. It replies in Arabic when the customer writes in Arabic, including Gulf dialect, and in English when they write in English. We set the Arabic to Gulf phrasing or Modern Standard Arabic as you prefer, test it on real messages from your chats and review the replies with your team before launch. Answers come only from your catalog and policies."},{"id":"k293","title":"WhatsApp Agent in the UAE: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Can customers pay with Tabby or Tamara in the chat? A: Not inside WhatsApp itself. The agent sends a link to your store's checkout, where customers choose Tabby, Tamara, a card or cash on delivery, as your store allows. Payment details never pass through the agent; it only sees from the order in your store whether it has been paid. Q: Where is the data stored? A: Chat history, logs and order lookups can be hosted in a UAE cloud region, or in the EU or US if you prefer. Messages pass through Meta's WhatsApp servers on the way, which your privacy notice should cover. Clinic chats with patient details stay in a UAE region."},{"id":"k294","title":"WhatsApp Agent in the UAE: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: We are in the DIFC or ADGM. What changes? A: The data protection law changes. DIFC firms follow the DIFC law and its Regulation 10, which asks for clear notice when someone first uses an AI system, so the agent opens each chat by saying it is an AI assistant. ADGM firms follow the ADGM Data Protection Regulations 2021, and onshore businesses the federal PDPL. Q: Can it send offers to all our WhatsApp contacts? A: Only to people who opted in to hear from you. Offers go out as Meta-approved marketing templates with an easy opt-out, and anyone who opts out is not messaged again. Messaging people who did not ask can hurt your number's quality rating, so we start with recent buyers and enquirers."},{"id":"k295","title":"WhatsApp Agent in the UAE: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uae/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Does it keep working in Ramadan and on Eid? A: Yes. The agent runs every day, including Fridays, weekends, Ramadan nights and Eid. We switch it to your Ramadan hours and delivery cut-offs, add iftar and suhoor timings for restaurants, and chats that need a person wait in your inbox until your team is back. Q: Does the agent phone customers? A: No. It works on WhatsApp and Instagram messages only. When a lead asks for a call, it books one of your team's call slots, and we set those between 09:00 and 18:00, the hours the UAE telemarketing rules allow for marketing calls."},{"id":"k296","title":"AI agents set up for one country (local rules, systems and prices): Receptionist Agent in ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/ai-receptionist/","text":"Our AI receptionist for UK businesses answers every call 24/7 in a natural British English voice, books into Dentally, Cliniko, Commusoft or your diary and puts urgent calls through to a person. It is set up for UK rules: privacy and recording information in the greeting, processor terms and UK hosting. Prices below in pounds. Local rules: UK GDPR Article 13, telling callers, Recording business calls (2018 Regulations), PECR regulation 19, automated marketing calls, PECR regulation 22, marketing texts. Systems: Dentally, Cliniko, Commusoft, simPRO, ServiceM8, Reapit, Clio, Google Calendar, Outlook, Calendly, HubSpot."},{"id":"k297","title":"Receptionist Agent in the UK: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: How much does the Receptionist Agent cost in the UK? A: Setup is about £1,150, then about £260 a month for hosting, monitoring, weekly tuning and a fair-use volume of usage. Usage above that (call minutes, WhatsApp conversation fees, AI model costs) is passed through at cost with no markup, and we tell you before it happens. Our prices are set in US dollars (US$1,500 + US$349/mo); local figures are approximate at £0.75 per US$1, November 2026, and your quote states the exact amount and currency. Q: Does it work with a UK 0333 number? A: Yes. You keep your 0333 number and your provider forwards calls to the agent, all the time, after hours or only when your lines are busy. The same works for local 01 and 02 numbers, 0800 freephone numbers and mobiles, and callers still dial the number they know."},{"id":"k298","title":"Receptionist Agent in the UK: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Do callers have to be told the call is recorded? A: Yes, and the greeting does it. When you turn recording on, every caller hears that the call is recorded and that they are speaking to an AI assistant before the conversation starts, with a pointer to your privacy notice. Your data protection lead confirms the wording. Q: Can it handle practices in England and Scotland with different bank holidays? A: Yes. Each site gets its own opening hours, bank holiday calendar and diary, so a Scottish branch can close on St Andrew's Day while an English branch stays open. Callers hear the hours for the site they rang."},{"id":"k299","title":"Receptionist Agent in the UK: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Can it tell NHS patients from private patients? A: Yes, if you want it to. We set it up to ask whether the caller is an NHS or private patient, offer slots from the matching appointment types and answer from the policies you approve. Questions about NHS eligibility or exemptions go to your team. Q: Can it send appointment reminders by text? A: Yes. Confirmations and reminders go out by text or WhatsApp with no promotional content. If you want marketing texts too, they go only to people who gave consent or fall under the soft opt-in, and every one offers a free way to opt out."},{"id":"k300","title":"Receptionist Agent in the UK: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/uk/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Does it understand strong regional accents? A: We test it with sample calls in the accents your callers use before go-live and tune it in the first weeks. If it still cannot understand a caller after a second try, it offers a person or a call back rather than guessing. Q: Is our callers' data kept in the UK? A: Yes, stored data is. Call recordings, transcripts and summaries are kept in a UK cloud region, we sign processor terms with you under Article 28 of the UK GDPR and your retention rules delete them automatically. Where your policy requires it, we pick voice and model providers that process calls in the UK or EU."},{"id":"k301","title":"AI agents set up for one country (local rules, systems and prices): Receptionist Agent in ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/ai-receptionist/","text":"Our AI receptionist for US businesses answers every call 24/7 in American English or Spanish, books into the dental, field-service or legal software you already use and transfers urgent calls. We set it up for US rules: a BAA for health data, a recording notice for all-party consent states and registered business texting. Prices below in US dollars. Local rules: HIPAA business associate agreements, Call recording in all-party consent states, AI voices on outbound calls (TCPA), Registered business texting (A2P 10DLC). Systems: Open Dental, Dentrix, athenahealth, DrChrono, ServiceTitan, Jobber, Housecall Pro, Clio, Google Calendar, Outlook, Calendly, HubSpot, Follow Up Boss."},{"id":"k302","title":"Receptionist Agent in the USA: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: How much does the Receptionist Agent cost in the USA? A: Setup is $1,500, then $349 a month for hosting, monitoring, weekly tuning and a fair-use volume of usage. Usage above that (call minutes, WhatsApp conversation fees, AI model costs) is passed through at cost with no markup, and we tell you before it happens. Your quote states the exact amount before any work starts. Q: Can it record calls in all-party consent states? A: Only with notice, and your lawyer decides whether that is enough. When you turn recording on, the greeting tells every caller that the call is recorded before the conversation starts, so callers in states such as Maryland, which require all parties' consent, know before they speak. If you prefer, recording stays off."},{"id":"k303","title":"Receptionist Agent in the USA: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Will you sign a BAA for our dental office or clinic? A: Yes. We sign a Business Associate Agreement with your practice before the agent handles any patient information, run it on providers that sign a BAA with us, keep PHI in a US region and out of model training, and document the data flow for your privacy officer. Q: Can it check a patient's insurance eligibility? A: Not by itself. It answers in-network questions from the plan list you approve and collects the carrier, member ID and date of birth, then your team or your existing eligibility tool verifies benefits. It never tells a caller what their plan will pay."},{"id":"k304","title":"Receptionist Agent in the USA: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Can it make reminder calls, or does it only answer? A: It answers inbound calls by default. Reminders go out by text, and if you also want reminder or callback calls, the agent dials only numbers with consent on record, because the FCC treats AI-generated voices as artificial voices under the TCPA. Q: Do we need to register our number to send texts? A: Yes, if the confirmations come from a standard local number. US carriers require A2P 10DLC registration for business texting from an application, so we register your brand and message types before go-live. A toll-free number goes through its own verification instead."},{"id":"k305","title":"Receptionist Agent in the USA: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/locations/usa/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Does it work with ServiceTitan, Jobber or Housecall Pro? A: Yes. We connect the agent through the software's API so it can create the customer, book the job with the address and problem, and see your technicians' availability. We test bookings with your dispatcher before go-live. Q: Can one agent answer offices in different states? A: Yes. Each location gets its own number, time zone, hours, holidays and calendar, and the agent answers with that location's details. Callers who want a different office are transferred or booked there."},{"id":"k306","title":"Free tools: AI visibility checker","url":"https://visionbotix.com/tools/ai-visibility-checker/","text":"free check of whether ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Google and Bing can crawl, read and identify a web page (robots.txt per AI crawler, noindex/nosnippet, text without JavaScript, structure, schema), with a score out of 100 and the top fixes. Includes a reference table of AI crawler user agents."},{"id":"k307","title":"Free tools: Project cost estimator","url":"https://visionbotix.com/estimate/","text":"price range, timeline and cost drivers for apps, websites, SaaS MVPs and AI agents."},{"id":"k308","title":"Our own products: Wakeel","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/wakeel/","text":"Wakeel is an AI legal matching platform built and run by Visionbotix. A person describes a legal problem in their own words, in Urdu, English or Roman Urdu, by typing or speaking. The AI works out the city, case type, court level and budget, then shows verified advocates who fit, with a plain explanation of why each one was matched. Live at https://www.wakeel.com.pk"},{"id":"k309","title":"Wakeel: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/wakeel/","text":"Q: What is Wakeel? A: Wakeel is an AI legal matching platform for Pakistan, built and operated by Visionbotix. People describe a legal problem in Urdu, English or Roman Urdu, and the AI matches them with verified advocates who fit their city, case type, court level and budget. Q: Does Wakeel give legal advice? A: No. Wakeel is a referral and matching platform. It helps people find a suitable, verified advocate; the advice comes from the advocate."},{"id":"k310","title":"Wakeel: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/wakeel/","text":"Q: How does the AI understand Roman Urdu? A: The AI is built for the way people in Pakistan actually write, including Roman Urdu and mixed Urdu and English. It extracts structured fields (city, practice area, court level, budget) from whatever the person writes or says, and those fields drive the search. Q: How are lawyers verified? A: Before a profile is listed, Wakeel checks active Bar Council enrollment, the advocate's disciplinary history, and their identity and office address."},{"id":"k311","title":"Wakeel: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/wakeel/","text":"Q: What does Wakeel show about Visionbotix? A: It is our own product, built end to end by our team. It shows how we build AI-first interfaces where one plain-language prompt replaces forms and filters, which is the same approach we use for client marketplaces, booking tools and support products. Q: Can you build a prompt-first product like this for my business? A: Yes. We build the prompt interface, the extraction and matching logic, the data model behind it and the admin tools, as a web or mobile app. Book a call and we will scope it, usually with a fixed quote within 24 hours."},{"id":"k312","title":"Our own products: VX-1 IP Encryptor","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"The VX-1 IP Encryptor is a hardware network encryptor from Visionbotix. It encrypts all IP traffic crossing your WAN with AES-256 in counter mode on dedicated FPGA silicon, with no operating system to attack. Place one unit at each end of a link and power on: it works transparently on Layer 2 and Layer 3 networks, including satellite links."},{"id":"k313","title":"VX-1 IP Encryptor: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"Q: What is the VX-1 IP Encryptor? A: It is a hardware network encryptor built by Visionbotix on dedicated FPGA silicon. It encrypts all IP traffic crossing a WAN with AES-256 in counter mode at near line-rate speed, deploys plug-and-play with zero configuration and has no operating system, which keeps its attack surface minimal. Q: How is the VX-1 deployed? A: You place one unit at each end of the link, connect it and power it on. It operates transparently at the IP layer, so your routers, switches and endpoints keep their current configuration."},{"id":"k314","title":"VX-1 IP Encryptor: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"Q: What networks does the VX-1 work on? A: It works on Layer 2 and Layer 3 networks, including ISP links, private WANs and satellite connections. It has been tested with multi-vendor routing and switching equipment in the path, across VLAN, hybrid and enterprise topologies. Q: Does the VX-1 run software that needs patching? A: No. It has no operating system, no background services and no software stack. Encryption runs entirely in FPGA hardware, which removes the patching, updates and configuration drift that software encryptors need."},{"id":"k315","title":"VX-1 IP Encryptor: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"Q: How is the VX-1 different from a software VPN? A: A software VPN runs on an operating system that needs patching and can be attacked. The VX-1 encrypts in FPGA hardware with no operating system, needs no configuration and keeps near line-rate throughput with low latency. Q: How was the encryption validated? A: The AES-256 output was checked byte for byte against the NIST FIPS 197 reference vectors. Performance was measured with the RFC 2544 and ITU-T Y.1564 test suites, and real web, DNS, FTP, SMTP, VoIP and video traffic was verified to pass uninterrupted."},{"id":"k316","title":"VX-1 IP Encryptor: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"Q: How much does the VX-1 cost? A: The VX-1 is quoted per deployment, based on the number of links and sites. Ask for a technical briefing and we will prepare a quote for your network."},{"id":"k317","title":"Our own products: ThreatIQ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"ThreatIQ is an internal defense layer for air-gapped and classified networks. One dedicated appliance with lightweight endpoint clients assesses vulnerabilities across six technology layers, detects insider threats with user behavior analytics and benchmarks configurations against the CIS Benchmarks. Everything runs offline, inside the air gap, and nothing leaves the network."},{"id":"k318","title":"ThreatIQ: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"Q: What is ThreatIQ? A: ThreatIQ is an internal defense platform by Visionbotix for air-gapped and classified networks. It combines vulnerability assessment across six technology layers, user behavior analytics for insider threat detection and compliance benchmarking against the CIS Benchmarks in one appliance. Q: Does ThreatIQ need an internet connection? A: No. ThreatIQ is built offline-first. It runs as a dedicated hardware appliance inside the protected LAN with lightweight clients on each endpoint, and all scanning, analytics and reporting happen inside the air gap. Nothing leaves the network."},{"id":"k319","title":"ThreatIQ: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"Q: What does ThreatIQ assess? A: Six layers, each assessed independently. These are malware exposure, third-party and custom software, operating systems, web applications against the OWASP Top 10, malicious network traffic, and services and ports following NIST SP 800-115. The results are combined into one report with prioritized remediation. Q: How does ThreatIQ detect insider threats? A: Lightweight endpoint clients monitor user activity across eight behavioral criteria, matched against over 1,000 specific event patterns. Unusual or malicious activity is flagged early so your security team can respond before it escalates."},{"id":"k320","title":"ThreatIQ: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"Q: Does ThreatIQ work on segmented networks? A: Yes. It supports segmented architectures, including networks split into two lines by a physical or logical air gap. Q: Does ThreatIQ integrate with our existing tools? A: ThreatIQ is self-contained, so the appliance and its endpoint clients are all it needs to run. If you want it to work alongside tools you already use, we scope that during the technical briefing."},{"id":"k321","title":"ThreatIQ: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"Q: How is ThreatIQ priced? A: ThreatIQ is quoted per deployment, based on the size and layout of your network. Ask for a briefing or a demo and we will prepare a quote."},{"id":"k322","title":"Our own products: Cyber Range","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"The Visionbotix Cyber Range is a training and testing platform for security teams. Red and blue teams practice attack and defense on realistic simulated internet traffic, and switches, routers, firewalls and IDS/IPS are benchmarked against standards such as RFC 2544 and RFC 3511 before you buy. We design the range, deliver it and train your operators."},{"id":"k323","title":"Cyber Range: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"Q: What is a cyber range? A: A cyber range is to IT security what a firing range is to marksmanship. It is a safe, realistic environment where security teams practice attack and defense, and where network devices are tested before they are deployed. Q: What can be tested on the Visionbotix Cyber Range? A: Switches and routers per RFC 2544 and RFC 2889, firewalls and next-generation firewalls per RFC 3511 and the BMWG methodology, Layer 4 to 7 applications, application servers, IDS/IPS, DLP and antimalware systems. Tests run on realistic simulated internet traffic, attack libraries and traffic replayed from your own applications."},{"id":"k324","title":"Cyber Range: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"Q: How do red team and blue team exercises work? A: A red team equipped with professional penetration testing and vulnerability scanning tools attacks infrastructure that a blue team defends with firewalls, IDS/IPS and SIEM. Attacks use real vulnerabilities such as DDoS and SQL injection on simulated traffic, so nothing real is harmed. Q: Does the Cyber Range include training? A: Yes. We deliver customized training on network design, performance testing, attack theory and firewall and IPS deployment, plus dedicated ongoing support. Schedules and plans are agreed with each customer."},{"id":"k325","title":"Cyber Range: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"Q: Is the traffic on the range real internet traffic? A: It is simulated, but built to be indistinguishable from the real thing. The range generates business, streaming, gaming, social and peer-to-peer traffic from IANA-allocated address space, with any country selectable as source or target, so teams train on realistic conditions while nothing real is harmed. Q: Can we get reports or connect the range to our own tools? A: Yes. The range produces PDF, Word and HTML reports with graphs and charts, and offers a RESTful API for custom integrations and automation."},{"id":"k326","title":"Cyber Range: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"Q: How is the Cyber Range priced? A: Each range is quoted per deployment, based on the teams you train, the devices you test and the training you need. Ask for a briefing and we will prepare a proposal."},{"id":"k327","title":"Our own products","url":"https://visionbotix.com/","text":"- [Smart Livestock](https://livestock.visionbotix.com) - [Vision AI cameras](https://cv.visionbotix.com)"},{"id":"k328","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Genetic sample colle","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/genetic-sample-collection-platform/","text":"A genetics research programme studying inherited disorders. We built a complete sample-management platform for a genetics research programme: an offline-first iPhone and iPad app for questionnaires, pedigree building, document scans and geotagging, plus a companion app that records 3D facial models with Apple's TrueDepth camera, all linked to one family record and synced to a central back office."},{"id":"k329","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Multi-vendor marketp","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/multi-vendor-marketplace-platform/","text":"A multi-vendor marketplace operator. We built a full multi-vendor marketplace: an installable web storefront, customer and rider mobile apps, vendor dashboards, a point-of-sale app and an admin console, all on one inventory. AI tools speed up listing and discovery, and the platform runs in three languages with right-to-left support, designed for low-cost phones."},{"id":"k330","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Touch-free consultat","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/gesture-controlled-consultation-kiosk/","text":"A hair and skin treatment clinic. We built a touch-free consultation kiosk for a hair and skin clinic: a standalone desktop app that runs an interactive quiz and is controlled entirely by hand gestures. Webcam-based computer vision tracks the visitor's hand and turns it into pointer movement, clicks and scrolling, with no touch, keyboard or mouse."},{"id":"k331","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI patient-intake an","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/ai-patient-triage-assistant-clinic-network/","text":"A telehealth clinic network. An AI intake and triage assistant for a telehealth clinic network. Patients describe their symptoms, an LLM pipeline built with LangChain asks adaptive follow-up questions, classifies urgency and the likely department, and gives doctors a ranked summary on a dashboard with history, flags and exportable reports."},{"id":"k332","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Edge AI visual inspe","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/edge-ai-manufacturing-defect-detection/","text":"An industrial parts manufacturer. A real-time visual inspection system for an industrial parts manufacturer. A computer-vision model trained on the factory's own images runs on a Raspberry Pi with a camera at the line, flags defective parts as they pass, alerts supervisors and keeps an inspection log with images. No cloud is involved."},{"id":"k333","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): No-code chatbot buil","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/whatsapp-web-chatbot-builder-platform/","text":"A customer-support software business. A no-code chatbot builder sold as SaaS. Users design FAQ, lead-capture and ticketing bots in a drag-and-drop flow editor, publish them to WhatsApp through Twilio or to a website widget, and track every conversation in an analytics dashboard. Flows can be exported and imported between accounts."},{"id":"k334","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI smart dairy farm ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/ai-smart-dairy-farm/","text":"Our own product for dairy and livestock farms. Our Smart Livestock product turns a dairy farm into a data-driven operation. Computer vision and IoT sensors record every animal's weight, temperature, milk production, fat content and feed each day, and a dashboard flags health and yield problems early, so farmers act before small issues become expensive."},{"id":"k335","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Field workforce atte","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/field-workforce-attendance-app/","text":"A municipal waste-management company. We built an attendance and location app for a waste-management company whose staff mostly work in the field. Employees mark attendance on their phones, the app logs location in the background every hour, and supervisors see in one view who is in the office, who is on route, and the full history."},{"id":"k336","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI monitoring and at","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/campus-monitoring-robots/","text":"A client running campuses, offices and public-sector facilities. We built two computer-vision robots for campuses and public spaces. The monitoring robot detects smoking, fire, crowding and missing masks and sends alerts with photo evidence. The attendance robot recognises people at the entrance and records attendance and body temperature without contact."},{"id":"k337","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Contactless temperat","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/contactless-temperature-screening/","text":"A client with offices, factories and retail sites. We built an autonomous temperature-screening station: it detects each person's face, measures body temperature without contact, and saves every reading with a photo in date-organised records. Businesses get fast entry checks and an audit trail ready for any inspection, with no staff needed at the door."},{"id":"k338","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Autonomous explorati","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/autonomous-exploration-mapping-robot/","text":"A robotics research and development client. Our autonomous robot explores spaces it has never seen. It heads for the edge of its current map (frontier-based exploration), labels rooms and objects with computer vision as it builds the map (semantic fusion), and calculates the shortest route home, with no prior map and no human guidance."},{"id":"k339","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI remote exam proct","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/ai-remote-exam-proctoring-platform/","text":"An education provider running remote exams. A remote exam proctoring system for an education provider. It watches webcam, audio and typing behavior during the exam, checks identity with anti-spoofing face detection and keystroke biometrics, flags anomalies in real time, keeps an offline backup of answers and produces an integrity report with heatmaps afterwards."},{"id":"k340","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI task assistant fo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/slack-ai-task-assistant-for-teams/","text":"A team-productivity software startup. An AI task assistant for teams. People describe work in plain language in Slack and the assistant creates the task, assigns it, predicts a deadline and priority, runs standups, sends reminders and syncs with Notion. Managers get a performance insights view without asking anyone for a status update."},{"id":"k341","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Real-time fleet trac","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/real-time-fleet-tracking-dashboard/","text":"A logistics operator running a vehicle fleet. A real-time fleet management dashboard for a logistics operator. It shows every vehicle live on a map, supports geofences and route playback, alerts on speeding, harsh braking and idling, and turns fuel data into reports. The streaming backend was built to handle hundreds of vehicles reporting at once."},{"id":"k342","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Retail demand foreca","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/retail-demand-forecasting-inventory-platform/","text":"A retailer with multiple product categories. A demand forecasting and inventory optimization platform for a multi-category retailer. Machine-learning models trained on sales history forecast demand with seasonality, simulate stock depletion and raise reorder alerts automatically. Buyers work from category dashboards and export the numbers for planning."},{"id":"k343","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Offline voice-to-voi","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/offline-voice-translation-mobile-app/","text":"A consumer mobile-app business. A mobile app that translates speech to speech, even without a connection. It chains speech recognition, translation and text-to-speech, uses compressed on-device models for offline language packs, and keeps conversation history in a chat-style view stored only on the phone, with no cloud sync."},{"id":"k344","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Gym management platf","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/gym-management-platform-member-app/","text":"A gym and fitness business. A gym management platform with a member mobile app. Staff manage members, trainers, schedules and payments in one back office; trainers upload workout and nutrition plans and chat with members in the app; renewal and payment reminders go out automatically, with billing handled by Stripe."},{"id":"k345","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Smart-grid monitorin","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/smart-grid-monitoring-fault-prediction/","text":"An electricity utility. A smart-grid monitoring system for an electricity utility. Low-power LoRa sensors stream readings into a time-series database, real-time dashboards show the state of the network, and anomaly-detection models predict faults and raise alerts. A REST API lets other utility systems use the data."},{"id":"k346","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Face-recognition ent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/face-recognition-access-attendance-system/","text":"A company managing access to its offices. A face-recognition entry and attendance system for offices. A Raspberry Pi terminal recognizes staff with anti-spoofing checks, logs attendance from each entry, alerts on unknown faces and unauthorized attempts, and keeps running offline. Managers review access and attendance in a reporting dashboard."},{"id":"k347","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI SEO article gener","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/ai-seo-blog-content-generator/","text":"A content-marketing software startup. A generative AI writing product for SEO content. Users enter a topic, a keyword planner suggests terms with difficulty and volume, a GPT-4 pipeline built with LangChain drafts the article, an SEO audit checks it, and the result exports to HTML, Markdown or WordPress."},{"id":"k348","title":"Resources (guides, cost guides and comparisons): AI agent vs chatbot: what is the differen","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agent-vs-chatbot/","text":"A chatbot answers questions in a conversation. An AI agent finishes tasks: it plans the steps, uses your tools, such as the order system, calendar or CRM, and acts within limits you set, with a person approving risky actions. Choose a chatbot when answers are enough and an agent when customers need something done. Our chat agents start from $1,500 setup + $299/month. By Sikandar Farooq, updated 2026-11-20."},{"id":"k349","title":"AI agent vs chatbot: what is the difference, and which do you need?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agent-vs-chatbot/","text":"Q: Is ChatGPT a chatbot or an AI agent? A: Both, depending on how it is set up. In a plain chat window it is an assistant that answers and writes. When it is given tools, such as web browsing, code execution or access to your apps, and allowed to work through several steps on its own, it behaves like an agent. The label depends on what it is allowed to do, not on the model underneath. Q: Is an AI agent more expensive to run than a chatbot? A: Usually a little, because an agent makes more model calls per conversation (it plans, calls tools and checks results) and needs integrations kept alive. The bigger cost difference is setup: connecting your systems, writing the rules for each action and testing them. With us, packaged agents run $750–$3,500 to set up, and the monthly fee covers hosting, monitoring and tuning."},{"id":"k350","title":"AI agent vs chatbot: what is the difference, and which do you need?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agent-vs-chatbot/","text":"Q: Can an AI agent work without any human oversight? A: It can, but for customer-facing work it should not at first. We start agents in a staged rollout, review every conversation in week one, and keep refunds, cancellations and deletions behind an approval gate unless you decide to relax it. You widen what it may do alone only after the logs show it is reliable. Q: Do I need to replace my existing chatbot to get an agent? A: Not always. If your chat widget or help desk allows a custom bot or an API connection, the agent can sit behind the same widget and inbox your customers already use. What changes is the brain and the access behind it, not the channel."},{"id":"k351","title":"AI agent vs chatbot: what is the difference, and which do you need?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agent-vs-chatbot/","text":"Q: What is conversational AI, and how does it relate to agents? A: Conversational AI is the broad term for software that talks with people in natural language, by text or voice. Modern chatbots and voice assistants are conversational AI. An AI agent often has a conversational front end too, but the conversation is only the interface: the defining part is that it can take actions in other systems."},{"id":"k352","title":"Resources (guides, cost guides and comparisons): AI agents glossary: 45 terms explained in","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agents-glossary/","text":"This AI agents glossary explains 45 terms in plain English, from agent and LLM to RAG, MCP, guardrails and prompt injection. If you read only six ideas, read these: agents act through tools, MCP connects those tools, RAG grounds answers in your data, approvals limit actions, evals measure quality and red teaming finds weaknesses. By Sikandar Farooq, updated 2026-11-20."},{"id":"k353","title":"AI agents glossary: 45 terms explained in plain English: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agents-glossary/","text":"Q: Do I need to understand all these terms to buy an AI agent? A: No. You need the handful in this guide's six sections: what the agent may do on its own, where its answers come from, which systems it connects to, who approves risky actions, how quality is measured and how it was tested against attacks. A good provider explains the rest as it comes up. Q: Should I use RAG or fine-tuning for my company's data? A: Usually RAG. It answers from your current documents, cites its sources and updates when a document changes. Fine-tuning helps when you need a fixed format, tone or narrow skill, or a smaller model that is cheaper to run. Many production systems use RAG alone, and some combine the two."},{"id":"k354","title":"AI agents glossary: 45 terms explained in plain English: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agents-glossary/","text":"Q: Can an AI agent work without sending our data to a model provider? A: Yes. An open-weight model can run on your own servers or in your private cloud, so prompts and documents never leave your environment. The trade-off is that you run and update the model yourself, and the strongest models are often available only through a provider's API. Q: How do you stop an AI agent from making things up? A: You cannot get the risk to zero, but you can make it small and visible: answer only from approved sources, show citations, let the agent say it does not know, hand off to a person when unsure, and run evals on real questions before and after every change."},{"id":"k355","title":"AI agents glossary: 45 terms explained in plain English: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agents-glossary/","text":"Q: What does MCP change for a business? A: Instead of building a separate integration for each AI tool, you build one MCP server for a system such as your CRM, and Claude, ChatGPT, Copilot and other clients can all use it. The security work, scopes and audit logs then live in one place."},{"id":"k356","title":"Resources (guides, cost guides and comparisons): Build vs buy AI agents: custom, off-the-s","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/build-vs-buy-ai-agents/","text":"Buy a SaaS agent when the job is standard and lives inside a tool you already use. Choose a packaged, managed agent ($750–$3,500 setup with us) when the job is common but runs on your own tools and rules. Build custom, from $8,000, when the workflow sets you apart, the data is sensitive or per-use pricing gets expensive at your volume. By Sikandar Farooq, updated 2026-11-20."},{"id":"k357","title":"Build vs buy AI agents: custom, off-the-shelf or packaged?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/build-vs-buy-ai-agents/","text":"Q: Is it cheaper to build your own AI agent? A: Rarely in the first year. The model calls are cheap; the cost is people: engineers to build the integrations, write tests, watch the agent and keep it working as models and APIs change. Building pays off when the agent is central to how you compete, or when your volume makes per-seat or per-use pricing expensive. Q: Can a packaged agent be customized? A: Yes, within its job. Ours are set up on your tools, trained on your content, written in your tone and given your approval rules. What a packaged agent does not do is change its job: if you need a different process, that is a custom agent."},{"id":"k358","title":"Build vs buy AI agents: custom, off-the-shelf or packaged?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/build-vs-buy-ai-agents/","text":"Q: What do I keep if I stop paying for a managed agent? A: With us, monthly plans run month to month after any minimum term in your quote, and you keep your data and the configuration we built for you. With a custom build, the contract assigns the code, prompts and configuration to you on payment. Ask any vendor the same question in writing before you sign. Q: Should a startup build its own AI agent framework? A: Usually not. Open-source frameworks and model providers already handle the agent loop, tool calling and tracing. Spend your engineering time on what is specific to you: the integrations, the rules, the evaluation set built from your real cases and the product around the agent."},{"id":"k359","title":"Build vs buy AI agents: custom, off-the-shelf or packaged?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/build-vs-buy-ai-agents/","text":"Q: How long does each option take to go live? A: A SaaS agent inside a tool you already use can be switched on quickly, then needs your content and rules. Our packaged agents go live in about two weeks, or two to four weeks when your documents must be loaded and tested. A custom agent takes six to ten weeks for a first production release."},{"id":"k360","title":"Resources (guides, cost guides and comparisons): How much does an AI agent cost in 2026?","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agent-cost/","text":"A packaged AI agent costs $750–$3,500 to set up and $199–$499 a month to run with us, and it goes live in two to four weeks. A custom agent built around your own systems starts from $8,000 at a fixed price. Agency quotes for custom agents commonly run from five figures into six, so start with one scoped job. By Sikandar Farooq, updated 2026-11-20."},{"id":"k361","title":"How much does an AI agent cost in 2026?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agent-cost/","text":"Q: What is the cheapest way to get an AI agent? A: A packaged agent for one job, such as answering calls or replying to reviews. Ours start from $750 setup + $199/month. You get the same engineering as a custom build, but the scope, integrations and guardrails are already worked out, so you pay for setup and tuning instead of design. Q: Why does an AI agent have a monthly fee? A: An agent is not finished at launch. The monthly fee pays for hosting, monitoring, weekly tuning on real conversations, guardrail updates and a fair-use volume of model and call usage. Usage above that is passed through at cost with no markup, and we tell you before it happens."},{"id":"k362","title":"How much does an AI agent cost in 2026?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agent-cost/","text":"Q: How much does a custom AI agent cost? A: With us, from $8,000 at a fixed price agreed after scoping. The price grows with the number of systems it connects to, how much it may do without a human, the languages and channels it covers, and how strict your compliance needs are. Q: Can I build an AI agent myself with a no-code tool? A: Yes, for a simple internal workflow. The tool subscription is cheap; the real cost is your time on integrations, testing edge cases, guardrails and keeping it working when a model or API changes. Most businesses that start this way bring in help once the agent touches customers or money."},{"id":"k363","title":"How much does an AI agent cost in 2026?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-agent-cost/","text":"Q: How long does it take to build an AI agent? A: Our packaged agents go live in about two weeks, or two to four weeks for agents that need your documents or data loaded and tested. Custom agents take six to ten weeks for a first production release."},{"id":"k364","title":"Resources (guides, cost guides and comparisons): How much does an AI receptionist cost in ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-receptionist-cost/","text":"Our AI receptionist costs $1,500 setup + $349/month, with call usage above a fair-use volume passed through at cost. Self-serve AI apps cost less a month but leave the setup and tuning to you, and human answering services bill per call or minute, so they cost more at volume. Compare options on cost per answered call. By Sikandar Farooq, updated 2026-11-20."},{"id":"k365","title":"How much does an AI receptionist cost in 2026?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-receptionist-cost/","text":"Q: Is there a free AI receptionist? A: Some self-serve tools have a free tier with a small number of calls a month. It is a good way to hear the technology, but free tiers often do not include calendar booking, call transfer rules or someone checking how calls went, which is where most of the value is. Q: Do I pay for calls the AI receptionist cannot handle? A: With us, a call the agent transfers to your team is still a call it answered: it greets the caller, takes the reason and passes a summary. Setting up transfers and escalation rules is part of the setup; the minutes of a live transfer count toward your call usage."},{"id":"k366","title":"How much does an AI receptionist cost in 2026?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-receptionist-cost/","text":"Q: Can I try it before I pay for setup? A: Yes. Call the live demo from your browser: it answers as a fictional dental clinic, checks a test calendar and books you in. On a free 30-minute call we then map your call types and send a fixed quote within 24 hours. Q: Is the Clinic Front Desk bundle cheaper than the receptionist alone? A: Not cheaper than one agent, but cheaper than the three agents bought one by one. It costs $3,000 setup + $699/month and includes the Receptionist Agent, Booking Agent and Reputation Agent, so calls, new-lead follow-up, reminders and review requests run together."},{"id":"k367","title":"How much does an AI receptionist cost in 2026?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/ai-receptionist-cost/","text":"Q: Do I need a new phone number? A: No. You keep your number and forward calls to the agent: all calls, only after hours, or only when your lines are busy. If you want a new local number, the carrier charge is a third-party cost passed through at cost."},{"id":"k368","title":"Resources (guides, cost guides and comparisons): How much does it cost to build an app in ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/app-development-cost/","text":"With us, a web app starts from $3,000, an iOS and Android app from $8,000 and a SaaS MVP from $12,000, each at a fixed price after scoping. Published agency ranges run from a few thousand dollars for a simple app into six figures for a complex one. Features, integrations, platforms and compliance set the price. By Sikandar Farooq, updated 2026-11-20."},{"id":"k369","title":"How much does it cost to build an app in 2026?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/app-development-cost/","text":"Q: Is it cheaper to build a web app or a mobile app? A: Usually a web app. With us a web app starts from $3,000 and an iOS and Android app from $8,000, because mobile adds device testing, store submission and two platforms to support. A progressive web app is a good first step when users mainly need forms, browsing and notifications. Q: Can I pay for an app in stages? A: Yes. We quote a fixed price and split it into milestones, such as scope and design, the core build and the store launch. You pay for each milestone after it works, so you never pay far ahead of what you can see."},{"id":"k370","title":"How much does it cost to build an app in 2026?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/app-development-cost/","text":"Q: Does the price include the back end and admin panel? A: For our mobile apps, yes: the \"from\" price covers the app for iOS and Android from one codebase, the back end, an admin panel, testing on real devices and store submission. Hosting and third-party services are billed at cost, separately. Q: How accurate is an online app cost calculator? A: It gives you a range, not a price. Ours uses the same cost drivers we quote with, so it lands close for typical projects, but integrations and edge cases only show up in scoping. After a free call we send a fixed quote within 24 hours, and that is the price you pay."},{"id":"k371","title":"How much does it cost to build an app in 2026?: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/app-development-cost/","text":"Q: Who owns the app and the code? A: You do. The code, the designs, the store accounts and the signing keys are yours, created in your name, so releases never depend on us and you can move to another team at any time."},{"id":"k372","title":"Resources (guides, cost guides and comparisons): n8n vs custom AI agents: when a workflow ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/n8n-vs-custom-ai-agents/","text":"n8n is enough when the job is a clear sequence of steps between apps, with one or two AI steps, moderate volume and someone technical to look after it. Choose custom code when the AI has to reason across many steps, needs tests and version control, runs at high volume or acts on money and customers. Many teams use both. By Sikandar Farooq, updated 2026-11-20."},{"id":"k373","title":"n8n vs custom AI agents: when a workflow tool is enough: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/n8n-vs-custom-ai-agents/","text":"Q: Is n8n open source? A: Not in the strict sense. The code is public on GitHub, but it is licensed under n8n's own Sustainable Use License, which limits use to your own internal business, non-commercial or personal purposes. n8n describes it as fair-code. For most companies automating their own work that makes no practical difference; it matters if you want to resell n8n itself. Q: Can an agency build n8n workflows for us without breaking the license? A: Yes. n8n's license FAQ says consulting and automation services are permitted, including charging for building and maintaining workflows. What the license rules out is giving outside users the ability to build or edit workflows inside a product. With us, the workflows run in your own n8n account or self-hosted instance."},{"id":"k374","title":"n8n vs custom AI agents: when a workflow tool is enough: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/n8n-vs-custom-ai-agents/","text":"Q: Is n8n good enough for customer-facing AI agents? A: For a simple assistant with a few tools and a human approval step, it can be. Once the agent talks to many customers, handles money or needs repeatable test results before each change, the testing and release discipline of code starts to matter more than the speed of the visual editor. Q: Should we pick n8n or Make? A: Pick n8n if your data has to stay in your own cloud or you want a flat cost at high volume by self-hosting. Pick Make if a non-developer will own the workflow and you value its large set of ready connectors. Both handle branching and AI steps well enough for most back-office work."},{"id":"k375","title":"n8n vs custom AI agents: when a workflow tool is enough: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/n8n-vs-custom-ai-agents/","text":"Q: What does it cost to have you build an n8n workflow? A: Our Ops Agent, built in n8n, Make or custom code, costs $2,000 setup + $299/month and goes live in about two weeks. If you only want the first workflow built and handed over, AI automation projects start from $2,000. Custom agents start from $8,000."},{"id":"k376","title":"Resources (guides, cost guides and comparisons): Software outsourcing in 2026: Pakistan vs","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/pakistan-vs-india-vs-eastern-europe-outsourcing/","text":"Pakistan usually has the lowest published rates, India has the deepest market and the largest vendors, and Eastern Europe costs more but shares European hours and, inside the EU, European data law. Pick on overlap, data rules and the team you will actually get, not the country. Our own rates start at $25 an hour. By Sikandar Farooq, updated 2026-11-20."},{"id":"k377","title":"Software outsourcing in 2026: Pakistan vs India vs Eastern Europe: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/pakistan-vs-india-vs-eastern-europe-outsourcing/","text":"Q: Is it safe to outsource software development to Pakistan? A: It is as safe as the contract and the setup you agree. Keep the code in your own repository, give access per person through your own accounts, sign an NDA and an IP assignment before work starts, and use test data instead of live records. Ask any vendor how they keep working through a power or internet cut, and expect a specific answer. Q: Should I choose a big vendor or a small studio? A: A large vendor gives you bench strength, many specialist skills and formal processes, which suits big programs. A smaller studio usually gives you senior people and the founder within one email. For a product team of two to ten people, ask each option who exactly will write your code and whether you can interview them."},{"id":"k378","title":"Software outsourcing in 2026: Pakistan vs India vs Eastern Europe: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/pakistan-vs-india-vs-eastern-europe-outsourcing/","text":"Q: Do I need a company or office in my own country to work with an offshore team? A: No. Most offshore teams invoice you directly from their own country under a services contract. What you do need is a clear contract: the governing law, how disputes are settled, who owns the IP, the notice period and how data is handled. With us, US clients get a W-8BEN-E and UK clients get invoices without UK VAT. Q: Fixed price or time and materials? A: Fixed price per milestone suits a scoped first release, because you know the cost before work starts. A monthly dedicated team suits a product with a moving roadmap. Many teams start with one fixed-price milestone to test a vendor, then move to a dedicated team once trust is there."},{"id":"k379","title":"Software outsourcing in 2026: Pakistan vs India vs Eastern Europe: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/pakistan-vs-india-vs-eastern-europe-outsourcing/","text":"Q: Can I split work between two countries? A: Yes, and some companies do it to spread risk, for example a European team for work that touches EU personal data and an Asian team for the rest. It adds coordination cost, so keep one owner for architecture and code review, and one shared repository and backlog."},{"id":"k380","title":"Resources (guides, cost guides and comparisons): What is MCP (Model Context Protocol)? A p","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/what-is-mcp/","text":"MCP (Model Context Protocol) is an open standard that lets AI apps such as Claude, ChatGPT, Copilot and Cursor connect to tools and data in one consistent way. You build an MCP server once in front of a system, and every app that supports MCP can use it. Anthropic created it; it now sits in the Linux Foundation's Agentic AI Foundation. By Sikandar Farooq, updated 2026-11-20."},{"id":"k381","title":"What is MCP (Model Context Protocol)? A plain-English guide: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/what-is-mcp/","text":"Q: Is MCP only for Claude? A: No. Anthropic created MCP, but it is an open standard, donated to the Agentic AI Foundation under the Linux Foundation, and ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot Studio, VS Code, Cursor and Gemini CLI can all connect to MCP servers. One well-built server works with all of them. Q: Does MCP replace our APIs? A: No. An MCP server usually calls your existing API underneath. It adds a layer designed for AI: a short list of clearly described tools, per-user sign-in and a consistent way for any AI app to discover and call them. Your API stays the source of truth."},{"id":"k382","title":"What is MCP (Model Context Protocol)? A plain-English guide: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/what-is-mcp/","text":"Q: Do I need to be a developer to use MCP? A: To use one, no. In Claude or ChatGPT you add a connector by pasting the server address and signing in. To build a server that is safe for company data, yes: scopes, OAuth, approvals and logging are engineering work. Q: Can I just use an open-source MCP server from GitHub? A: For personal experiments, often yes, after reading the code. For company data, check that it supports per-user sign-in, narrow permissions and an audit log, pin the version you reviewed, and run it in a sandbox. Some public servers use one broad token, which most security teams will not accept."},{"id":"k383","title":"What is MCP (Model Context Protocol)? A plain-English guide: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/resources/what-is-mcp/","text":"Q: How much does a custom MCP server cost? A: Our MCP Connector costs $2,500 as a one-off project, delivered in two to four weeks. You get the source code, OAuth sign-in, approval gates for writes, audit logging and security testing. An optional maintenance plan keeps it current as the specification and AI clients change."},{"id":"k384","title":"Company","url":"https://visionbotix.com/","text":"- [About](https://visionbotix.com/about/) - [How we work](https://visionbotix.com/process/) - [Industries](https://visionbotix.com/industries/) - [Where we work](https://visionbotix.com/locations/) - [Resources](https://visionbotix.com/resources/) - [Pricing](https://visionbotix.com/pricing/)"},{"id":"k385","title":"Company","url":"https://visionbotix.com/","text":"- [Project cost estimator](https://visionbotix.com/estimate/) - [Contact](https://visionbotix.com/contact/) - [Careers](https://visionbotix.com/careers/) - [Privacy policy](https://visionbotix.com/privacy/) - [Terms of use](https://visionbotix.com/terms/)"}];
